E["item:99-year-old-port"] = {t="item",n="99-Year-Old Port",z="wailing",s="At Ratchet's docks, a bottle of 99-Year-Old Port has gone missing. Mad Magglish took it in a cargo spill and fled toward the Wailing Caverns.",h="At Ratchet's docks, a bottle of 99-Year-Old Port has gone missing.",sec={{t="A High-Value Cargo Spill",b="Crane Operator Bigglefuzz overloaded his crane while unloading a large shipment from Booty Bay in Ratchet. Crates crashed across the docks. In the confusion, Mad Magglish seized a bottle of 99-Year-Old Port and fled into the hills toward the Wailing Caverns.",sp=0},{t="Diplomatic Vintage",b="Baron Revilgaz of the Blackwater Raiders sent the port to Gazlowe, Ratchet’s chief engineer and ruler, as a diplomatic gift. Its loss threatens Bigglefuzz’s livelihood and strains relations with the dockmaster. Mad Magglish lurks in the outer grottos of the caverns with the unopened bottle. The dockhands seek mercenaries to recover it before Gazlowe learns of the blunder.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who was the 99-Year-Old Port originally meant for?",a="Baron Revilgaz, master of Booty Bay, sent the bottle as a personal gift to Gazlowe, Ratchet’s boss.",al={"who is the port for","who gets the port","gazlowe gift"},it="why_wanted"},{q="How did Mad Magglish end up with the port?",a="Bigglefuzz overloaded his crane while unloading cargo, scattering crates across Ratchet’s docks. Mad Magglish seized the bottle amid the confusion and ran.",al={"how was it stolen","who stole the port","dock mishap"}},{q="Where did Mad Magglish take the bottle?",a="Magglish fled inland across the Barrens and hid in the rocky antechambers and outer tunnels leading into the Wailing Caverns.",al={"where is mad magglish","where is the port hidden","port location"},it="place"},{q="Why didn't Bigglefuzz retrieve the port himself?",a="Bigglefuzz pursued Magglish to the threshold of the Wailing Caverns, but refused to enter. He feared the beasts and corrupted druids inside.",al={"why bigglefuzz not chase","crane operator coward"},it="motive"},{q="What is the 99-Year-Old Port?",a="It is an exceptionally rare and aged bottle of fortified wine shipped all the way from Booty Bay. Sent as a prestigious personal gift from Baron Revilgaz to Gazlowe, the chief engineer and leader of Ratchet, this vintage represents an invaluable token of esteem between powerful goblin trade barons.",al={"what is 99-year-old port","99 year old port","bottle of port"},it="identity",add="5b0242c9"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="Mad Magglish uses amateur stealth to hide in the dark outside the Wailing Caverns. As a rogue, you can flush him from the shadows."},kw={"99-year-old port","bigglefuzz","gazlowe","mad magglish","port","ratchet","revilgaz","wailing caverns"},rel={"quest:959","npc:crane-operator-bigglefuzz","npc:baron-revilgaz","subzone:ratchet","zone:wailing","zone:barrens","subzone:booty-bay"},src={"99-Year-Old Port","Trouble at the Docks"}}
E["item:deviate-hide"] = {t="item",n="Deviate Hide",z="wailing",s="In the Wailing Caverns, Deviate Hide bears the mark of Naralex's dream. Druids seek to turn its taint to useful leather goods.",h="In the Wailing Caverns, Deviate Hide bears the mark of Naralex's dream.",sec={{t="Tainted Pelts of the Nightmare",b="Naralex's slumber beneath the Barrens changed the beasts of the Wailing Caverns. The night elf druid's dream became an Emerald Nightmare, and deviate predators arose with tough, mutated hides. Their pelts carry evil, yet remain supple and resilient for leathercrafting.\n\nNalpak gathers the hides from his perch high above the cavern mouth, in a skull-shaped rock formation. He studies their properties and fashions them into sturdy utility packs.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What makes a deviate hide different from normal leather?",a="The Emerald Nightmare that seeps from Naralex's slumber warped the beasts that bear deviate hides. Their flesh is strangely durable and elastic, unlike ordinary beast pelts.",al={"deviate hide lore","why are deviate hides weird","deviate pelt nature"},it="identity"},{q="Who is collecting these hides?",a="Nalpak collects the hides. A disciple of Naralex, he camps in the eye-socket cave above the Wailing Caverns' entrance. He believes the deviate beasts' wicked materials can be redeemed as useful leather goods.",al={"who wants deviate hides","nalpak hides","who needs deviate hide"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where are deviate hides found?",a="Deviate hides come from beasts prowling inside the Wailing Caverns beneath the Barrens, including raptors, vipers, crocolisks, and dreadfangs.",al={"where do deviate hides drop","how to get deviate hides"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Where does Deviate Hide come from, and who made it?",a="Deviate hides are taken from the strange, warped beasts that roam deep within the Wailing Caverns. These creatures were not crafted by mortal hands; rather, they arose from beneath the Barrens, mutated by the foul nightmare that consumed the druid Naralex as he fell into his deep slumber. The unnatural corruption altered the native wildlife, granting their skins strange and otherworldly qualities.",al={"where do deviate hides come from","deviate hide origin","who made deviate hide"},it="origin",add="8b5833f5"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you can see the Emerald Nightmare's corruptive power over nature in these hides. Nalpak seeks to redeem the corrupted materials for practical survival."},kw={"barrens","deviate hide","leather","nalpak","naralex","nightmare","pelts","wailing caverns"},rel={"npc:nalpak","quest:1486","zone:wailing","npc:naralex","zone:barrens"},src={"Deviate Hide","Deviate Hides (Classic)"}}
E["item:gem-of-anacondra"] = {t="item",n="Gem of Anacondra",z="wailing",s="In the Wailing Caverns, Lady Anacondra bears one of four dream gems held by the corrupted serpent leaders. The stones are bound to the nightmare spreading through the Barrens.",h="In the Wailing Caverns, Lady Anacondra bears one of four dream gems held by the corrupted serpent leaders.",sec={{t="A Corrupted Focus",b="When Naralex fell into deep slumber, he sought to bring water and life back to the arid Barrens. Then the Emerald Nightmare entered his thoughts and twisted his closest disciples. Lady Anacondra and her fellow conspirators left their old ways and became the Druids of the Fang. Their purpose was to restore the land, but it turned into a toxic delusion.\n\nLady Anacondra carries one of four dream gems held by these serpent leaders. The gem focuses their corrupted bond with the Emerald Dream and anchors the nightmare within the cave system.",sp=0},{t="Cleansing the Vision",b="Nara Wildmane and the Cenarion druids in Thunder Bluff suffer visions in their sleep. The wicked faces of the Fang's leaders haunt them. They claim the Gem of Anacondra and the stones of Cobrahn, Pythas, and Serpentis to confirm Lady Anacondra has been struck down. Gather all four, and the oppressive nightmare can lift from the minds of Kalimdor's keepers of balance.",sp=1,bt={"q886.6"}}},faq={{q="What is the Gem of Anacondra?",a="Lady Anacondra carries the Gem of Anacondra in the Wailing Caverns. It is one of four dream gems held by the leaders of the corrupted Druids of the Fang.",al={"what is anacondra gem","anacondra gem","what does gem of anacondra do"},it="identity"},{q="Who wants this gem?",a="Nara Wildmane, a tauren druid on the Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff, seeks this gem and the other three dream gems. She hopes to free her mind from nightmares and protect the Barrens.",al={"who takes gem of anacondra","where do i turn in anacondra gem","gem of anacondra turn in"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where can the Gem of Anacondra be found?",a="Lady Anacondra carries the gem in the winding underground tunnels of the Wailing Caverns in the central Barrens.",al={"where does it drop","who drops gem of anacondra","lady anacondra location"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Why are the dream gems important?",a="The corrupted leaders of the Druids of the Fang hold the four gems. Gathering them confirms the ringleaders have been eliminated and breaks their hold over the Emerald Dream's corruption in the region.",al={"why four gems","purpose of dream gems","leaders of the fang gems"},it="power"},{q="Where does the Gem of Anacondra come from, and who made it?",a="The gem is carried by Lady Anacondra deep within the Wailing Caverns. While the exact master who cut or enchanted it is unknown, it serves as one of the dream gems held by the four leaders of the Druids of the Fang. Once part of a noble circle dedicated to healing the Barrens, these corrupted night elves now channel their twisted visions of the Emerald Dream into these stones.",al={"origin gem of anacondra","who made gem of anacondra","where did anacondra get her gem"},it="origin",add="2e0de493"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a Cenarion druid, you have a solemn duty to strike down a sister who surrendered her mind and forms to the corrupting Emerald Nightmare.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you aid Nara Wildmane of Thunder Bluff by recovering the gem. Then the dark visions that plague the Shu'halo's sleep on the Elder Rise may lift."},kw={"dream gem","druids of the fang","gem of anacondra","lady anacondra","leaders of the fang","nara wildmane","wailing caverns"},rel={"npc:lady-anacondra","quest:914","zone:wailing","topic:druids-of-the-fang","item:gem-of-cobrahn","item:gem-of-pythas","item:gem-of-serpentis","zone:thunderbluff"},src={"Gem of Anacondra","Leaders of the Fang"}}
E["item:gem-of-cobrahn"] = {t="item",n="Gem of Cobrahn",z="wailing",s="In the Wailing Caverns, Lord Cobrahn bears a dream gem shaped by corruption. Nara Wildmane needs it as proof of his defeat.",h="In the Wailing Caverns, Lord Cobrahn bears a dream gem shaped by corruption.",sec={{t="A Focus of Corrupted Dreams",b="Naralex entered the Emerald Dream to restore Kalimdor's barren plains. His nightmare twisted the Wailing Caverns and turned his disciples from their purpose. Cobrahn forsook the peaceful ways of the Cenarion Circle and took the shape of a serpent. He now carries one of four dream gems that anchor the leaders' hold over the subterranean waterways. Through it, he channels twisted dreams that threaten to make the Barrens a venomous marsh.",sp=0},{t="Restoring Balance",b="Nara Wildmane, a tauren druid in Thunder Bluff, suffers nightmares sent by the rogue Druids of the Fang. She seeks to cleanse the subterranean springs and protect Kalimdor from their vision. Lord Cobrahn and his three conspirators each hold a dream gem. Returning Cobrahn's gem to the Cenarion druids ends his corrupting influence over the sleeping Naralex.",sp=1,bt={"q886.6"}}},faq={{q="What is the Gem of Cobrahn?",a="In the Wailing Caverns, Lord Cobrahn carries the Gem of Cobrahn. The dream gem channels his nightmare-twisted power.",al={"gem of cobrahn","cobrahn gem","what is cobrahn gem"},it="identity"},{q="Who wants the Gem of Cobrahn?",a="Nara Wildmane, a tauren druid on the Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff, wants the Gem of Cobrahn and three others to end the Druids of the Fang.",al={"who needs gem of cobrahn","cobrahn gem turn in","who takes cobrahn gem"},it="why_wanted"},{q="How many gems are needed to complete the quest?",a="Four gems are needed: the Gem of Cobrahn, the Gem of Anacondra, the Gem of Pythas, and the Gem of Serpentis. Each is held by one of the four serpent leaders in the caverns.",al={"how many dream gems","leaders of the fang gems","all fang gems"},gp=true},{q="Who is Lord Cobrahn?",a="Lord Cobrahn was once a disciple of Naralex. When Naralex's vision became a nightmare, Cobrahn and several other druids took serpent form and formed the Druids of the Fang.",al={"who is cobrahn","lord cobrahn lore","cobrahn"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a Cenarion druid, reclaiming the Gem of Cobrahn marks the tragic but necessary end of a fallen brother who left nature's harmony for the Emerald Nightmare.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you know the druids of Thunder Bluff watch the Barrens closely. Taking Cobrahn's gem directly protects the plains and hunting grounds from unnatural corruption."},kw={"dream gem","druids of the fang","gem of cobrahn","leaders of the fang","lord cobrahn","nara wildmane","wailing caverns"},rel={"quest:914","npc:lord-cobrahn","topic:druids-of-the-fang","item:gem-of-anacondra","item:gem-of-pythas","item:gem-of-serpentis","zone:wailing","zone:thunderbluff"},src={"Gem of Cobrahn","Leaders of the Fang"}}
E["item:gem-of-pythas"] = {t="item",n="Gem of Pythas",z="wailing",s="In the Wailing Caverns, Lord Pythas bears one of four corrupted dream gems. Together, the gems feed the nightmare twisting the underground oasis and threaten the Barrens.",h="In the Wailing Caverns, Lord Pythas bears one of four corrupted dream gems.",sec={{t="A Vessel of the Nightmare",b="Naralex entered the Emerald Dream to restore the arid Barrens. There, his vision became a living nightmare. His foremost followers fell with him and became the Druids of the Fang. Now they seek to remake the surface world as a venomous jungle.\n\nLord Pythas bears one of four dream gems that anchor the corruption in the caverns. The stone channels the druids’ dark design. It also proves to the druids of Thunder Bluff that Pythas’s twisted trance has been broken.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Gem of Pythas used for?",a="Take the gem to Nara Wildmane in Thunder Bluff with the gems of Cobrahn, Anacondra, and Serpentis. Together, the four gems complete the work of ending the rogue leaders of the Druids of the Fang.",al={"gem of pythas use","what to do with gem of pythas","pythas gem quest"},it="purpose"},{q="Who carries this gem?",a="Lord Pythas carries the gem. He is a fallen night elf druid who dwells deep in the Wailing Caverns of the Barrens.",al={"who drops gem of pythas","pythas location","where to get gem of pythas"},it="target"},{q="Why do the druids of Thunder Bluff want the gem?",a="The corruption from the Wailing Caverns haunts Nara Wildmane and the Cenarion druids in Thunder Bluff. Securing the gems proves the four aberrant leaders are slain and cuts off the nightmare before it spreads farther into the Barrens.",al={"why does nara want gems","nara wildmane pythas"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Are there other gems like this one?",a="Yes. Each of the four leaders carries a dream gem deep in the cavern. The others are Lady Anacondra, Lord Cobrahn, and Lord Serpentis.",al={"other dream gems","fang gems","wailing caverns gems"},it="ties"},{q="What is the Gem of Pythas?",a="The Gem of Pythas is one of four dream gems carried by the leaders of the Druids of the Fang within the Wailing Caverns. Held by Lord Pythas, this relic embodies the dark, serpentine madness that corrupted these once-noble night elves, binding their twisted visions of the Emerald Dream into physical form.",al={"gem of pythas","what is gem of pythas","what is this gem"},it="identity",add="3d8d64d3"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a Cenarion druid, recovering the gem is a somber duty. It marks how far Naralex’s inner circle has fallen into serpentine horrors.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you know the twisted rites in the caverns threaten the Barrens’ fragile balance. Recovering these gems is vital to protecting your shamans’ and druids’ homeland."},kw={"barrens","dream gem","druids of the fang","gem of pythas","lord pythas","nara wildmane","wailing caverns"},rel={"npc:lord-pythas","quest:914","zone:wailing","topic:druids-of-the-fang","item:gem-of-cobrahn","item:gem-of-anacondra","item:gem-of-serpentis","zone:thunderbluff"},src={"Gem of Pythas","Leaders of the Fang"}}
E["item:gem-of-serpentis"] = {t="item",n="Gem of Serpentis",z="wailing",s="Deep in the Wailing Caverns, Lord Serpentis keeps the Gem of Serpentis close. The enchanted dream gem binds his will to the corrupted vision reshaping the caverns and threatening the Barrens.",h="Deep in the Wailing Caverns, Lord Serpentis keeps the Gem of Serpentis close.",sec={{t="Heart of the Serpentine Dream",b="Naralex fell into slumber in the Wailing Caverns, and the Emerald Nightmare reached him there. His most devoted followers became the fanatical Druids of the Fang. Lord Serpentis leads one part of the cabal, with three other leaders beside him. Each carries an enchanted dream gem, binding their shared will to the corrupted vision. Recovering Serpentis's gem breaks his hold over the caverns' life and strikes at the leaders directing corruption across the Barrens.",sp=0},{t="Proof for Thunder Bluff",b="The tauren druids on Thunder Bluff's Elder Rise suffer vivid nightmares from corruption beneath the savannah. Nara Wildmane is among those troubled. The gems of Serpentis, Cobrahn, Anacondra, and Pythas prove that the rogue order's leaders have fallen. Recovering them eases the nightmare's hold on the Cenarion Circle in Mulgore.",sp=1,bt={"q886.6"}}},faq={{q="Where does the Gem of Serpentis come from?",a="Lord Serpentis carries the gem deep in the winding waterways of the Wailing Caverns. He leads one of the four groups of Druids of the Fang.",al={"who drops gem of serpentis","where to get serpentis gem","serpentis gem location"},it="origin"},{q="What is the purpose of the gem?",a="The gem is one of four that the Druids of the Fang's leaders use to channel the nightmare warping the subterranean oasis. Nara Wildmane in Thunder Bluff seeks it as proof that Lord Serpentis has been defeated.",al={"why do i need gem of serpentis","what is gem of serpentis for"},it="purpose"},{q="Who wants all four dream gems?",a="Nara Wildmane asks you to bring her the gems of Cobrahn, Anacondra, Pythas, and Serpentis. She is a druid on the Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff. Together, the gems can sever the nightmare's hold over the region.",al={"who takes the gems","turn in serpentis gem","leaders of the fang turn in"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who was Lord Serpentis before carrying this gem?",a="Lord Serpentis was once a disciple of Naralex who entered the caverns to restore lush life to the Barrens. The Emerald Nightmare twisted his hopes into a fanatical desire to remake the world in serpent form.",al={"lord serpentis lore","who is serpentis"},it="identity"},{q="What is the Gem of Serpentis?",a="The Gem of Serpentis is one of four dream gems held by the leaders of the Druids of the Fang within the Wailing Caverns. Carried by Lord Serpentis himself, it serves as an emblem and instrument of the corrupted druids who seek to twist the Barrens to match their dark visions.",al={"gem of serpentis lore","what is serpentis gem","lord serpentis gem"},it="identity",add="58ca37b7"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you can see the danger in Serpentis and his cabal's dream gems. Deep communion with the Dream demands vigilant spiritual discipline.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you know that breaking Serpentis's hold on the gem helps free Thunder Bluff's shamans and druids from the dark visions disturbing their sleep across Mulgore."},kw={"druids of the fang","gem of serpentis","leaders of the fang","lord serpentis","nara wildmane","the barrens","wailing caverns"},rel={"npc:lord-serpentis","quest:914","topic:druids-of-the-fang","zone:wailing","quest:1490","item:gem-of-anacondra","item:gem-of-cobrahn","item:gem-of-pythas"},src={"Gem of Serpentis","Leaders of the Fang"}}
E["item:serpentbloom"] = {t="item",n="Serpentbloom",z="wailing",s="Deep in the Wailing Caverns, Serpentbloom has drawn the Royal Apothecary Society’s keen interest for its potent natural properties.",h="Deep in the Wailing Caverns, Serpentbloom has drawn the Royal Apothecary Society’s keen interest for its...",sec={{t="A Rare Subterranean Flora",b="In the Barrens, Serpentbloom thrives in the shadowy, damp tunnels of the Wailing Caverns. Unrestrained Emerald Dream energies have warped the caverns’ ecosystem. Venomous serpents often nest among the herb’s stems.\n\nHostile beasts and corrupted druids overrun the caves. Few who venture inside return with viable specimens.",sp=0},{t="Apothecary Interest",b="At the Pools of Vision beneath Thunder Bluff, Apothecary Zamah gathers Serpentbloom for the Royal Apothecary Society in Undercity. The Forsaken seek virulent, strange, chemically potent plants across Kalimdor to fuel research for the Dark Lady.\n\nZamah believes a harvest of Serpentbloom in significant quantities could bring valuable breakthroughs in Forsaken alchemy.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does Serpentbloom grow?",a="Serpentbloom grows only deep inside the Wailing Caverns, a labyrinthine network southwest of the Crossroads in the Barrens. It clings to the ground in the cavern’s dark, damp recesses.",al={"where to find serpentbloom","serpentbloom location","wailing caverns herb"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does the Royal Apothecary Society want Serpentbloom?",a="Apothecary Zamah, an agent of the Royal Apothecary Society stationed in Thunder Bluff, seeks Serpentbloom for research. The Forsaken study unusual and dangerous flora across Kalimdor to develop new chemical concoctions and advance the Society’s broader goals in service to Sylvanas Windrunner.",al={"who wants serpentbloom","apothecary zamah herb","why collect serpentbloom"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why is harvesting Serpentbloom hazardous?",a="The Wailing Caverns crawl with raptors, crocolisks, and corrupted druids. Serpentbloom often shelters venomous snakes, which may strike when the herb is disturbed.",al={"serpentbloom danger","serpentbloom snake"},it="danger",gp=true},{q="Can herbalists find Serpentbloom more easily?",a="Yes. Herbalists are naturally attuned to spotting vegetation, and can track Serpentbloom patches in the cavern’s shadowy corners.",al={"find serpentbloom herbalism","tracking serpentbloom"},gp=true},{q="What is Serpentbloom?",a="Serpentbloom is an exceedingly rare specimen of flora native to the darkest recesses of the Wailing Caverns in the Barrens. Rooted within the damp, subterranean depths, this unusual herb is distinguished by its serpent-like qualities—disturbing it often draws out aggressive snakes nestled around its roots.",al={"what is serpentbloom","serpentbloom herb","serpentbloom info"},it="identity",add="bee22cd2"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an undead, gathering Serpentbloom aids Apothecary Zamah and the Royal Apothecary Society as they seek botanical assets in foreign lands to strengthen the Forsaken.",["profession:Herbalism"]="As a herbalist, your trained eye can find rare cavern blooms where others see only damp stone."},kw={"apothecary zamah","barrens","herb","royal apothecary society","serpentbloom","thunder bluff","wailing caverns"},rel={"quest:962","quest:853","zone:wailing","zone:barrens","zone:thunderbluff","topic:royal-apothecary-society","topic:forsaken","zone:undercity"},src={"Serpentbloom","Serpentbloom (quest)"}}
E["item:wailing-essence"] = {t="item",n="Wailing Essence",z="wailing",s="In the Wailing Caverns, Wailing Essence gathers within roaming ectoplasms. Alchemists seek its potent properties, while nearby druids dread the mutations spreading through the Barrens.",h="In the Wailing Caverns, Wailing Essence gathers within roaming ectoplasms.",sec={{t="A Volatile Concoction",b="Beneath the central Barrens, unnatural energy twists beasts and gives rise to gelatinous ectoplasms. Within them lies a viscous substance called Wailing Essence. Nearby druids watch the waters with growing dread, while goblin traders see a chance for profit.\n\nIn Ratchet, Mebok Mizzyrix believes the essence is the missing ingredient for a lucrative line of “smart drinks” meant to sharpen the mind. The eccentric alchemist gives little thought to the corruption they might carry.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does Wailing Essence come from?",a="Wailing Essence comes from ectoplasmic slimes in the Wailing Caverns. Devouring ectoplasms, evolving ectoplasms, and nightmare ectoplasms all hold it.",al={"wailing essence drop","where to get wailing essence","what drops wailing essence"},it="origin"},{q="Who wants this essence?",a="Mebok Mizzyrix, a goblin experimenter in Ratchet, wants the essence for a new formula of his intellect-boosting “smart drinks.”",al={"who needs wailing essence","who buys wailing essence","wailing essence turn in"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is the essence suspected of doing to the Barrens?",a="Mebok suspects the essence makes wildlife mutate rapidly and unnatural plant growth spread across the Barrens.",al={"what does wailing essence do","is wailing essence dangerous","wailing essence lore"},it="power"},{q="Is drinking Wailing Essence actually safe?",a="Drinking Wailing Essence is reckless. It comes from corrupt, nightmare-tainted ectoplasms deep in a cursed cavern, yet Mebok plans to put it in a commercial drink.",al={"can you drink wailing essence","is smart drink safe"},it="danger"},{q="What is Wailing Essence?",a="Wailing Essence is a strange, potent substance found deep within the Wailing Caverns. It gathers inside the cavern's roaming ectoplasms and oozes, suspected by local observers of being the unnatural catalyst behind the bizarre mutations altering plants and wildlife throughout the surrounding Barrens.",al={"what is wailing essence","wailing essence info","about wailing essence"},it="identity",add="387b8d38"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you can read Wailing Essence as a sign of corruption deep within the Wailing Caverns and of the urgent need to cleanse the Dream’s taint."},kw={"ectoplasm","mebok mizzyrix","ratchet","smart drinks","wailing caverns","wailing essence"},rel={"quest:1491","npc:mebok-mizzyrix","zone:wailing","subzone:ratchet","quest:865","zone:barrens"},src={"Wailing Essence","Smart Drinks"}}
E["npc:crane-operator-bigglefuzz"] = {t="npc",n="Crane Operator Bigglefuzz",z="wailing",s="At Ratchet's docks, Crane Operator Bigglefuzz scrambles to recover cargo spilled from a crane. He searches for a stolen bottle before his superiors discover the loss.",h="At Ratchet's docks, Crane Operator Bigglefuzz scrambles to recover cargo spilled from a crane.",sec={{t="Mishap on the Docks",b="Crane Operator Bigglefuzz rushes to clear the wreckage across Ratchet's wharves. Like many goblin dockworkers, he chose speed over safety. While lifting an overloaded haul from a merchant vessel, his crane buckled and crates crashed across the docks. Scoundrels seized the confusion and swept up goods. Now he must recover the most precious cargo before Gazlowe or the local port masters dock his pay.",sp=0},{t="The Stolen Port",b="The greatest loss was a crate of rare ninety-nine-year-old port. Before Bigglefuzz could secure the spilled cargo, Mad Magglish, an elusive vagrant, snatched a bottle and hid. Bigglefuzz may have to answer for losing something irreplaceable.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Crane Operator Bigglefuzz?",a="Crane Operator Bigglefuzz loads and unloads sea cargo at Ratchet's docks for the Steamwheedle Cartel.",al={"who is bigglefuzz","crane operator","bigglefuzz ratchet"},it="identity"},{q="What caused the accident at the docks?",a="Bigglefuzz overloaded his crane while hoisting cargo. The machinery failed and spilled freight across the wharf.",al={"why did the crane drop cargo","ratchet dock accident","crane mishap"},it="history"},{q="Who stole from Bigglefuzz?",a="Mad Magglish seized the confusion from the spilled freight, snatched a valuable bottle of ninety-nine-year-old port, and slipped away.",al={"who took the port","mad magglish cargo","who robbed bigglefuzz"},it="threat"},{q="Why is Bigglefuzz so worried about the stolen bottle?",a="The ninety-nine-year-old port is extraordinarily rare and expensive. Losing it through negligence could bring severe financial penalties or worse from the Steamwheedle Cartel bosses.",al={"why does bigglefuzz care about the wine","trouble at the docks reason"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Whose side is Crane Operator Bigglefuzz on?",a="Bigglefuzz works for the Steamwheedle Cartel out of the neutral port of Ratchet. Like most goblins in town, his primary loyalty is to his trade and his employers rather than the Horde or the Alliance, welcoming any adventurer willing to do business or fix a costly mistake.",al={"bigglefuzz faction","who does bigglefuzz work for","crane operator bigglefuzz allegiance"},it="side",add="acbd2274"},{q="What does Crane Operator Bigglefuzz want?",a="Bigglefuzz wants someone to recover the bottle of 99-Year-Old Port that went missing when his cargo spilled all over the docks. A goblin named Mad Magglish made off with the rare vintage, and Bigglefuzz is desperate to get it back before his superiors discover the mishap.",al={"what does bigglefuzz need","bigglefuzz goal","what does bigglefuzz want you to do"},it="wants",add="e72c0e10"},{q="Why is Crane Operator Bigglefuzz here?",a="Bigglefuzz is stationed at the Ratchet docks to operate the heavy loading crane, transferring shipments between merchant vessels and the shore. Unfortunately, an attempt to hoist far too much cargo at once left his crane mangled and the port's freight scattered across the wharf.",al={"why is bigglefuzz in ratchet","bigglefuzz purpose ratchet","why is bigglefuzz at the docks"},it="why_here",add="d46df1e8"},{q="Who is Crane Operator Bigglefuzz tied to?",a="Bigglefuzz is tied to the Steamwheedle Cartel, serving as part of Ratchet's dockside workforce. His current worries tie him directly to the thief Mad Magglish, who swiped valuable liquor from his spilled cargo.",al={"bigglefuzz connections","who is bigglefuzz affiliated with","bigglefuzz cartel"},it="ties",add="eaf0ddf2"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you know overloading Steamwheedle rigging and cranes causes most industrial accidents along Kalimdor's coastlines.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you know how quickly a thief like Mad Magglish can use dockside confusion to lift priceless contraband right under a goblin's nose."},kw={"bigglefuzz","cargo","crane operator","docks","mad magglish","port","ratchet","steamwheedle"},rel={"quest:959","subzone:ratchet","topic:goblin","zone:wailing"},src={"Crane Operator Bigglefuzz"}}
E["npc:ebru"] = {t="npc",n="Ebru",z="wailing",s="Above the Wailing Caverns, Ebru watches Naralex's dream turn to nightmare. A night elf druid and one of his few uncorrupted disciples, she calls on travelers to enter the depths and cull the mutated horrors born of the Nightmare.",h="Above the Wailing Caverns, Ebru watches Naralex's dream turn to nightmare.",sec={{t="A Watch Above the Descent",b="Ebru keeps watch from a camp inside the cavernous skull above the Wailing Caverns' entrance. Most of Naralex's followers have fallen to the emerald corruption spreading through the caverns, but she escaped it.\n\nNaralex hoped to draw on underground springs and make the arid Barrens a woodland. His plan has gone horribly wrong, and Ebru sees that dream become a nightmare. She urges willing travelers into the depths to kill the growing number of deviate beasts threatening the surrounding plains.",sp=0},{t="The Price of Corruption",b="The Nightmare has twisted the caves and Ebru's fellow disciples, making them the fanatical Druids of the Fang. Their companionship is gone, and her circle faces ruin. Ebru turns her efforts to containing the corruption.",sp=1,bt={"q886.5","q886.6"}}},faq={{q="Who is Ebru?",a="Ebru is a night elf druid and one of Naralex's few uncorrupted disciples. She watches from a cave high above the Wailing Caverns' entrance and coordinates efforts to stem the corruption spreading into the Barrens.",al={"who is ebru","ebru lore","about ebru"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Ebru located above the Wailing Caverns?",a="Ebru fled to the crag above the cave entrance when Naralex's ritual collapsed into the Emerald Nightmare and turned her fellow disciples into hostile zealots. From her perch, she watches the caverns and stays safe from the feral horrors inside.",al={"where is ebru","why is ebru up here","ebru cave location"},it="why_here"},{q="What happened to Naralex and his other disciples?",a="Naralex entered a deep trance to tap the underground springs, but his mind became trapped in the Emerald Nightmare. The corruption twisted the cave's plants and animals and drove most of his disciples mad, turning them into the Druids of the Fang.",al={"what happened to the disciples","naralex fate","druids of the fang origin"},it="ties"},{q="What does Ebru ask travelers to do?",a="Ebru urges travelers to enter the depths of the Wailing Caverns and cull the deviate beasts. She wants them to strike back against the mutated horrors born from her master's tormented dreams.",al={"ebru quests","deviate eradication","cleansing the caverns"},it="wants"},{q="Whose side is Ebru on?",a="Ebru serves the Cenarion Circle and remains loyal to her mentor, the druid Naralex. Unlike many of her peers who fell prey to the nightmare invading the caverns, she has not turned hostile or succumbed to corruption. While she is a night elf, she will welcome any capable traveler—Alliance or Horde alike—willing to venture into the depths to purify the oasis and save her master.",al={"ebru faction","is ebru alliance or horde","who does ebru serve"},it="side",add="5ace5551"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For a druid of the Cenarion Circle, meeting Ebru is a stark reminder of the dangers of walking the Emerald Dream and the terrible cost of losing control.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, Ebru shows that a small, isolated enclave of your people lives deep in Kalimdor's arid heart, far from the ancient boughs of Ashenvale and Teldrassil."},kw={"barrens","cenarion circle","deviate","druid","ebru","naralex","wailing caverns"},rel={"zone:wailing","npc:naralex","quest:1487","zone:barrens","topic:night-elf"},src={"Ebru"}}
E["npc:lady-anacondra"] = {t="npc",n="Lady Anacondra",z="wailing",s="Deep in the Wailing Caverns, Lady Anacondra holds to the Druids of the Fang. She followed Naralex in his effort to heal the Barrens, but his communion with the Emerald Dream became a nightmare. It shattered her mind and turned her devotion toward remaking the land in the dream’s image.",h="Deep in the Wailing Caverns, Lady Anacondra holds to the Druids of the Fang.",sec={{t="From Disciple to Serpent",b="Lady Anacondra followed Naralex into the caverns as he sought the Barrens’ subterranean springs through the Emerald Dream. Then dark visions seized his mind, and the nightmare spread from the dreaming realm to his disciples. Her sanity broke. Her hope for the land became a cold, reptilian obsession.",sp=0},{t="A Fanglord in the Deep",b="Lady Anacondra guards the Wailing Caverns’ first chambers. She and the other Fanglords have cast aside the Cenarion Circle’s teachings and embraced the viper’s vicious ways. She wields lightning and nature magic, and keeps Naralex in his twisted sleep with slumbering trances. Above, the nightmare’s corruption still threatens the Barrens.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Lady Anacondra originally?",a="Lady Anacondra began as a night elf druid who followed Naralex in his effort to heal the Barrens. His nightmare corrupted his disciples.",al={"anacondra real name"},it="identity"},{q="Why did she turn against the Cenarion Circle?",a="A nightmare overcame Naralex’s attempt to reach the Emerald Dream beneath the Barrens. It infected his acolytes, corrupting Lady Anacondra and turning her toward the twisted dream.",al={"why is anacondra evil","how did she become a druid of the fang"},it="motive"},{q="What is her role in the Wailing Caverns?",a="Lady Anacondra is one of the four Fanglords leading the Druids of the Fang. She guards the caverns’ upper reaches and helps keep Naralex trapped in corrupted sleep as the Fang work to remake the land in their dream’s image.",al={"what does anacondra do","lady anacondra purpose","why kill anacondra"},it="purpose"},{q="Where can she be found inside the caverns?",a="Lady Anacondra roams the first large network of caverns near the Wailing Caverns’ entrance. She patrols among the raptors and serpents, moving between several resting places.",al={"anacondra location","where is lady anacondra","anacondra spawn"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What item is taken from her for the Cenarion Circle?",a="Lady Anacondra carries the Gem of Anacondra. Nara Wildmane, a druid in Thunder Bluff, needs the gem to break the Fanglords’ hold over the Barrens.",al={"gem of anacondra","leaders of the fang anacondra","anacondra quest item"},it="item"},{q="What powers does she wield in battle?",a="Lady Anacondra wields nature magic, striking from afar with bolts of lightning. She can also cast magical slumber to incapacitate invaders while her reptilian allies attack.",al={"anacondra abilities","anacondra spells","anacondra attacks"},it="power"},{q="Whose side is Lady Anacondra on?",a="Lady Anacondra stands with the Druids of the Fang, having abandoned her former loyalty to the Cenarion Circle. Corrupted by the Emerald Nightmare that engulfed her master Naralex, she now opposes her former kin and defends the madness festering within the Wailing Caverns.",al={"anacondra faction","who does lady anacondra serve","lady anacondra allegiance"},it="side",add="1a1ef870"},{q="What does Lady Anacondra want?",a="Corrupted along with her sanity, Lady Anacondra seeks to remake the land to match the Druids of the Fang's twisted dream. She guards the nightmare festering in the Wailing Caverns and works to spread it alongside her fellow Fanglords.",al={"what is anacondra trying to do","anacondra goal","anacondra motivations"},it="wants",add="ec4c22d8"},{q="Why is Lady Anacondra here?",a="She was one of the druids who followed the night elf druid Naralex on his mission to restore the arid Barrens. She went with him into the Wailing Caverns to tap the underground springs, only to become trapped and twisted when his dream turned to nightmare.",al={"why is anacondra in wailing caverns","how did anacondra get here","anacondra barrens mission"},it="why_here",add="f4df78aa"},{q="Who is Lady Anacondra tied to?",a="Lady Anacondra is tied directly to Naralex, the powerful druid she served as an acolyte before his nightmare broke her mind. She is also bound to the other Fanglords—such as Cobrahn and Serpentis—who rule the twisted cult of the Druids of the Fang alongside her.",al={"who is anacondra master","anacondra naralex connection","who leads anacondra"},it="ties",add="6f9b72fe"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For Cenarion druids, Lady Anacondra’s story is a tragedy. Her zeal to heal the land left her open to the nightmare that turned her communion into madness.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you may see a sister of Kaldorei lineage who cast aside her heritage and form to pursue a twisted serpentine dream. Her fate warns of dangers within the Emerald Dream.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you must protect the Barrens’ delicate lifelines from Lady Anacondra and the Fanglords. Removing her is critical to securing Crossroads and the nearby oases."},kw={"anacondra","barrens","druids of the fang","fanglord","gem of anacondra","lady anacondra","naralex","wailing caverns"},rel={"npc:naralex","topic:druids-of-the-fang","quest:914","zone:wailing","zone:barrens","topic:druid"},src={"Lady Anacondra"}}
E["npc:lord-cobrahn"] = {t="npc",n="Lord Cobrahn",z="wailing",s="Deep in the Wailing Caverns, Lord Cobrahn commands the corrupted Druids of the Fang. He was a night elf druid in Naralex's order, until the nightmare in the cavern springs claimed him. Now he guards the twisted labyrinth in a deadly serpent guise.",h="Deep in the Wailing Caverns, Lord Cobrahn commands the corrupted Druids of the Fang.",sec={{t="A Druid Corrupted",b="Lord Cobrahn once served Naralex in his druid order. When Naralex entered the Wailing Caverns beneath the Barrens, he hoped to draw upon the underground springs and restore life to the arid wastes. Cobrahn went with him. But Naralex's communion with the Emerald Dream decayed into a twisting nightmare, and Cobrahn's mind shattered with those of his brothers.",sp=0},{t="The Serpent's Embrace",b="The nightmare warped Cobrahn's shapeshifting into a predatory reptilian form unlike the totemic beasts of Cenarion tradition. In battle, he takes the guise of a deadly serpent. Venomous deviate pythons flank him, and a vicious claw marks his right hand. Cobrahn rules his part of the grottos and violently purges anyone who tries to break the nightmare's hold on the caverns.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Lord Cobrahn before he turned evil?",a="Before the nightmare claimed him, Cobrahn was a night elf druid in Naralex's order. He entered the Wailing Caverns with Naralex, hoping their springs could heal the Barrens.",al={"cobrahn real name","who is cobrahn"},it="origin"},{q="Why is he called Lord Cobrahn?",a="No account explains the name Lord Cobrahn. The title suits a druid twisted by the Wailing Caverns' nightmare into a lethal serpent form, with deviate pythons at his side. The other Fang leaders, Anacondra, Pythas and Serpentis, also bear serpentine names.",al={"why cobrahn","lord cobrahn name meaning"},it="name"},{q="Where can Lord Cobrahn be found?",a="Lord Cobrahn resides deep within the Wailing Caverns, a twisting underground network in the central Barrens. Deviate pythons and other beasts corrupted by the nightmare surround him.",al={"cobrahn location","where is lord cobrahn","cobrahn room"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why do adventurers need to defeat him?",a="Cobrahn leads the Druids of the Fang and carries the Gem of Cobrahn. Nara Wildmane of Thunder Bluff seeks the gem to break the Fang leaders' hold over the Barrens.",al={"why kill cobrahn","leaders of the fang cobrahn"},it="purpose"},{q="What unique physical traits does he possess?",a="Cobrahn is larger than ordinary night elves and bears a sharp claw on his right hand. In combat, he can transform completely into an oversized venomous snake.",al={"what does cobrahn look like","cobrahn appearance"}},{q="What is his connection to the other Druids of the Fang?",a="Cobrahn is one of the four Fanglords, alongside Lady Anacondra and their kin. All were druids in Naralex's order, entered the caverns with him, and fell together to the nightmare's twisting corruption.",al={"druids of the fang leaders","cobrahn and anacondra"},it="ties"},{q="Who is Lord Cobrahn?",a="Lord Cobrahn is one of the four corrupted leaders of the Druids of the Fang lurking deep within the Wailing Caverns. Once a night elf druid of Naralex's noble order, which hoped to heal the Barrens, he fell prey to the dark nightmare that consumed the caverns. Twisted by its corruption, he now wields venomous magic and takes the shape of a massive serpentine beast.",al={"who is cobrahn","lord cobrahn lore","jarlaxla"},it="identity",add="ffd3d503"},{q="Whose side is Lord Cobrahn on?",a="Lord Cobrahn serves the Druids of the Fang and the spreading nightmare within the Wailing Caverns. He has severed all allegiance to the Cenarion Circle and the night elf people, standing alongside Naralex's fallen disciples against any who dare enter to cleanse the corruption.",al={"cobrahn faction","who does cobrahn serve","lord cobrahn allegiances"},it="side",add="3feb6d50"},{q="Why is Lord Cobrahn here?",a="He originally entered the Wailing Caverns alongside Naralex, intending to tap into the subterranean waters and restore the Barrens to a lush paradise. When Naralex's Emerald Dream connection warped into a nightmare, the energies poisoned the minds of his disciples. Cobrahn succumbed completely, remaining in the caverns to guard the slumbering archdruid and foster the nightmare's venomous spawn.",al={"why is cobrahn in wailing caverns","why did cobrahn come here"},it="why_here",add="7ca4c072"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For druids, Cobrahn shows how the nightmare can warp shapeshifting away from natural balance.",["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, Cobrahn's fall is a bitter tragedy. A skilled brother of the Cenarion Circle abandoned his heritage and now leads monsters in the subterranean depths.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde adventurer, you seek Cobrahn to end the foul corruption leaking into the Barrens and protect Kalimdor's fragile plains."},kw={"cobrahn","deviate python","druids of the fang","fanglord","gem of cobrahn","lord cobrahn","wailing caverns"},rel={"zone:wailing","quest:914","npc:lady-anacondra","topic:cenarion-circle","topic:druid","topic:night-elf"},src={"Lord Cobrahn"}}
E["npc:lord-pythas"] = {t="npc",n="Lord Pythas",z="wailing",s="Deep in the Wailing Caverns, Lord Pythas guards Naralex's slumber. Once a night elf warrior in Naralex's personal guard, he now leads the corrupted Druids of the Fang. His skill in battle and serpent magic bar the way to his master.",h="Deep in the Wailing Caverns, Lord Pythas guards Naralex's slumber.",sec={{t="A Guardian Falls",b="Pythas joined Naralex's personal guard when the druid's expedition entered the Barrens' dry wastes. A seasoned night elf warrior, he studied druidism to help Naralex restore life to the arid realm. Yet discipline and valor could not shield him from the corruption hidden in the caverns' depths.",sp=0},{t="The Lethal Sentinel",b="Dark nightmares seized Naralex's connection to the Emerald Dream. Pythas and his fellow acolytes fell under their sway. He forsook his old loyalty and became a leader of the Druids of the Fang.\n\nSome serpent lords favor spells or beast forms. Pythas wields nature magic alongside deadly combat skill. Now he prowls the winding caverns and guards the nightmare's hold on the spring.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Lord Pythas?",a="Lord Pythas once served in Naralex's personal guard and studied druidism to aid his master's work in the Barrens. He was a night elf warrior.",al={"who is pythas","lord pythas lore"},it="identity"},{q="Why did he turn against Naralex?",a="Pythas turned against Naralex after a nightmare seized the archdruid's thoughts as he reached into the Emerald Dream to heal the Barrens. Corruption spread through Naralex's acolytes, stripping Pythas of his sanity and remaking him as a serpent lord.",al={"why is pythas evil","how did pythas go mad","why did he become druid of the fang"},it="conflict"},{q="What makes Pythas different from the other Fang leaders?",a="Pythas was a seasoned warrior before training as a druid, and he joins martial skill with nature magic. The other Fang leaders rely on nature magic and beast forms.",al={"pythas fighting style","pythas vs other leaders"}},{q="Why do adventurers need to defeat him?",a="Pythas guards one of four enchanted gems needed to free the Barrens from the Fang leaders' twisted dreams. Nara Wildmane, a druid in Thunder Bluff, seeks all four gems.",al={"leaders of the fang quest","gem of pythas"},it="target"},{q="Where can Lord Pythas be found?",a="Lord Pythas lurks in the deep chambers of the Wailing Caverns, among corrupted beasts and fellow Fang cultists.",al={"pythas location","where is pythas"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens to his gem?",a="After Pythas is defeated, the Gem of Pythas can be recovered from his remains. The four serpent lords' gems are brought to Nara Wildmane in Thunder Bluff as proof that the Fang's leadership has been broken.",al={"gem of pythas use","what is gem of pythas"},it="item"},{q="Whose side is Lord Pythas on?",a="Lord Pythas serves the Druids of the Fang. Once a devoted protector and acolyte of Naralex, the nightmare took hold of his mind and warped his loyalty. Now, he stands completely aligned with the rogue sect, wielding his blade and nature magic to safeguard the nightmare rather than shield the master he once swore to defend.",al={"pythas faction","pythas alliance","who does pythas serve"},it="side",add="be91010a"},{q="What does Lord Pythas want?",a="Driven mad by the nightmare infecting Naralex's slumber, Pythas seeks to defend the Wailing Caverns from anyone seeking to cleanse them. Stripped of his sanity, he desires only to vanquish intruders who threaten the nightmare's hold, turning his martial discipline and druidic power entirely toward preserving the corrupted domain.",al={"pythas goals","what is pythas trying to do","pythas motive"},it="wants",add="a058df7c"},{q="Why is Lord Pythas in the Wailing Caverns?",a="Pythas originally journeyed into the caverns as one of Naralex's personal guards during the effort to restore the Barrens. When Naralex's trance twisted into an inescapable nightmare, Pythas succumbed alongside the other disciples, remaining deep within the caves as a corrupted guardian of the Fang.",al={"why is pythas in wailing caverns","pythas location reason","how did pythas get here"},it="why_here",add="d8d94386"},{q="Who is Lord Pythas tied to?",a="Before his descent into madness, Pythas was one of the personal guards of the druid Naralex. He traveled into the underground springs to keep Naralex safe while learning druidism, though the pervasive corruption broke his mind and bound him to the rest of the twisted Leaders of the Fang.",al={"pythas naralex","pythas connections","who does pythas know"},it="ties",add="d87430fd"},{q="Why is Lord Pythas feared?",a="Lord Pythas is considered the most formidable of the Leaders of the Fang. Unlike many acolytes who rely solely on nature spells, Pythas was a seasoned warrior before taking up druidism. His combination of deadly melee combat prowess, sheer physical resilience, and dark druidic magic makes him exceptionally lethal to any expedition.",al={"is pythas dangerous","why is pythas tough","pythas strength"},it="fame",add="eb0bbb13"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, Pythas shows how corruption in the Emerald Dream can twist devotion to nature magic.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, remember that Pythas was a disciplined night elf fighter and personal protector before corruption took hold. Martial skill alone could not guard his mind.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf seeking to restore balance to Kalimdor's scarred soils, Pythas's fall to madness is a bitter sorrow."},kw={"druids of the fang","gem of pythas","leaders of the fang","lord pythas","naralex","pythas","wailing caverns"},rel={"zone:wailing","npc:naralex","topic:druids-of-the-fang","quest:914","topic:druid","topic:night-elf"},src={"Lord Pythas"}}
E["npc:lord-serpentis"] = {t="npc",n="Lord Serpentis",z="wailing",s="Deep in the Wailing Caverns, Lord Serpentis leads the Druids of the Fang. Once a mighty druid in Naralex's order, he fell to madness when Naralex's dream soured in the cavern springs. Now he helps command the serpent-worshipping sect near the corrupted Naralex, who lies slumbering.",h="Deep in the Wailing Caverns, Lord Serpentis leads the Druids of the Fang.",sec={{t="From Noble Druid to Serpent Lord",b="Before the cavern springs darkened, Serpentis held great power and prestige as a druid. He belonged to the noble order led by Naralex. Together, they hoped to heal the Barrens with the springs and the Emerald Dream. But Naralex's vision became a corrupting nightmare, and its rising madness took hold of Serpentis and the other druids.",sp=0},{t="A Lord of the Fang",b="Naralex's twisted dreams spread corruption through his followers. Serpentis and the others became the Druids of the Fang, abandoning Cenarion balance and the totem animals of old. Now they seek to remake the Barrens in the image of their twisted dreams instead of healing it. Serpentis shares leadership with Lady Anacondra, Lord Cobrahn and Lord Pythas.",sp=0},{t="The Final Obstacle",b="Deep in the winding caverns, Lord Serpentis guards one of the four dream gems carried by the rogue sect's leaders. To wake the trapped master or reclaim the waters of the Oasis, Serpentis must be defeated and his gem taken. Only then can the serpent's hold over the labyrinth be broken.",sp=1,bt={"q886.6"}}},faq={{q="Who is Lord Serpentis?",a="Deep in the Wailing Caverns, Lord Serpentis leads the Druids of the Fang. Once a night elf druid of great power and prestige in Naralex's order, he fell to Naralex's nightmare along with his fellow druids.",al={"who is serpentis","lord serpentis lore","serpentis background"},it="identity"},{q="Why did Serpentis turn evil?",a="Naralex's attempt to heal the Barrens through the Emerald Dream became a nightmare. Its corruption spread among the druids who followed him, turning Serpentis toward madness and serpent worship.",al={"why did serpentis turn","serpentis corruption","why is serpentis bad"},it="motive"},{q="What is his relationship to Naralex?",a="Serpentis once followed Naralex into the caverns as one of his noble druids. He became a leader of the Druids of the Fang, who now seek to remake the Barrens in the image of their twisted dreams.",al={"serpentis and naralex","is serpentis related to naralex","naralex apprentice"},it="ties"},{q="Why do players need to kill him?",a="Serpentis leads the Druids of the Fang. Defeating him breaks the sect's grip on the Wailing Caverns, secures his gem and clears a path toward awakening Naralex.",al={"why kill serpentis","leaders of the fang serpentis","gem of serpentis"},it="target"},{q="Who are the Druids of the Fang?",a="The Druids of the Fang are renegade night elf druids who followed Naralex into the Wailing Caverns. Corrupted by the Emerald Nightmare, they abandoned traditional druidic forms for the aspects, venoms and behaviors of serpents. Serpentis and the other fanglords lead them.",al={"druids of the fang lore","what are druids of the fang","fang druids"},it="people"},{q="Whose side is Lord Serpentis on?",a="Lord Serpentis is the leader of the Druids of the Fang. Corrupted by the nightmare consuming his mentor Naralex, he has abandoned the Cenarion Circle and the ideals of the night elves, turning entirely hostile to all who enter the caverns.",al={"lord serpentis faction","who does serpentis serve","serpentis allegiance"},it="side",add="1f07cf4d"},{q="What does Lord Serpentis want?",a="Once a druid of great power and prestige among Naralex's disciples, his mind was warped into madness by the nightmare. Now insane, he seeks to hold dominion over the caverns with his twisted followers, proclaiming himself the serpent king.",al={"serpentis goal","what does serpentis want","serpentis motives"},it="wants",add="e8a94e96"},{q="Why is Lord Serpentis in the Wailing Caverns?",a="Serpentis originally came to the Wailing Caverns as one of Naralex's druids, helping his mentor tap into the subterranean springs to restore the Barrens. When Naralex lost control of his dream and nightmare corruptions erupted, Serpentis fell victim to the psychic torment and remained inside to claim the caves as ruler of the Druids of the Fang.",al={"why is serpentis here","why is lord serpentis in wailing caverns","lord serpentis location reason"},it="why_here",add="33635f36"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, Serpentis shows the danger within the Emerald Dream. Even a druid of great power can be twisted when a noble vision becomes a nightmare.",["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, Serpentis and his followers bring painful disgrace. They were kaldorei scholars of great renown, but abandoned their sacred duty to nature and became monstrous serpent lords.",["race:Tauren"]="For tauren, Serpentis's corruption desecrates the Earth Mother's balance. It threatens the Barrens' fragile ecosystem with unnatural madness."},kw={"druids of the fang","gem of serpentis","leaders of the fang","lord serpentis","naralex","serpentis","wailing caverns"},rel={"npc:naralex","zone:wailing","quest:914","topic:druids-of-the-fang","topic:druid","topic:night-elf"},src={"Lord Serpentis"}}
E["npc:mutanus-the-devourer"] = {t="npc",n="Mutanus the Devourer",z="wailing",s="In the Wailing Caverns, Mutanus the Devourer haunts Naralex's sleeping mind as a pale, monstrous murloc. The creature emerged from the Emerald Nightmare, and must fall before Naralex can awaken.",h="In the Wailing Caverns, Mutanus the Devourer haunts Naralex's sleeping mind as a pale, monstrous murloc.",sec={{t="A Dreamer's Worst Fear",b="Naralex, a night elf druid, sought to restore the Barrens by joining its underground springs to the Emerald Dream. Instead, the Emerald Nightmare entered his thoughts. Trapped in an agonizing vision, Naralex's fears took shape through the corruption as an immense, albino murloc.",sp=0},{t="The Waking Nightmare",b="When a Disciple of Naralex begins the ritual to revive their master, Mutanus crosses from dream into waking life. The dark force in Naralex's mind sent him to keep the druid asleep. Until Mutanus falls, Naralex remains trapped in his own corrupted imagination.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Mutanus the Devourer?",a="Mutanus the Devourer is a huge, pale murloc-like creature born from the Emerald Nightmare. The aberration came into being in the corrupted mind of the sleeping druid Naralex.",al={"who is mutanus","what kind of creature is mutanus","is mutanus a murloc"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Mutanus look like a giant murloc?",a="Naralex's nightmare took the form of a colossal albino murloc. Why the corruption chose that shape is unknown.",al={"why murloc","why is mutanus a murloc","naralex murloc fear"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Mutanus appear at the end of the ritual?",a="The dark presence corrupting the Emerald Dream sent Mutanus to keep Naralex asleep. When the disciples begin the awakening ritual, Mutanus crosses into the physical cavern to devour those trying to save the druid.",al={"when does mutanus spawn","why summon mutanus","naralex ritual boss"},it="why_here"},{q="Where does Mutanus come from?",a="Mutanus comes from the Emerald Nightmare, the corrupted realm that has ensnared Naralex.",al={"mutanus origin","is mutanus from the nightmare","emerald nightmare mutanus"},it="origin"},{q="Does killing Mutanus save Naralex?",a="Yes. When Mutanus falls, the nightmare's immediate hold on Naralex's mind breaks. His disciples can then awaken him and end the cavern's dark trance.",al={"is naralex saved","what happens after mutanus dies","waking naralex"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why is Mutanus immune to shadow magic?",a="Mutanus is woven from dark nightmare energies and resists necrotic and shadow spells that would harm ordinary beasts.",al={"mutanus shadow immunity","shadow spells mutanus","is mutanus shadow immune"},it="power"},{q="Whose side is Mutanus the Devourer on?",a="Mutanus serves whatever dark, corrupting force has infected the Emerald Dream and trapped Naralex in his nightmare. Rather than acting on his own whims or serving the native wildlife of the Barrens, he obeys the will of the Nightmare itself, sent forth into the waking world solely to ensure the druid remains asleep and corrupted.",al={"who controls mutanus","mutanus faction","mutanus allegiance"},it="side",add="1d17d2ec"},{q="What does Mutanus the Devourer want?",a="Mutanus exists to disrupt any attempt to wake Naralex from his twisted slumber. He seeks to devour anyone who tries to liberate the sleeping druid from the Nightmare's grip, ensuring Naralex remains helpless while the dark corruption continues to fester within the Wailing Caverns.",al={"mutanus goal","why does mutanus fight","what is mutanus trying to do"},it="wants",add="93f250d8"},{q="Who is Mutanus the Devourer tied to?",a="Mutanus is directly tied to the night elf druid Naralex. He is not a natural beast born of the Barrens, but a physical manifestation born from the darkest corners of Naralex's own corrupted mind, embodying the druid's subconscious fears as a twisted nightmare in the physical world.",al={"mutanus connection naralex","mutanus relationship naralex","who is mutanus linked to"},it="ties",add="c0fe9c52"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you see the danger of entering the Emerald Dream without safeguards. Naralex's mind was overtaken by corruption.",["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei, Mutanus embodies the tragedy of Naralex's noble effort to heal the Barrens becoming a monstrous nightmare.",["faction:Horde"]="The Horde cannot let Mutanus and the Nightmare corrupt the heart of the Barrens, where vital oasis waters sustain Durotar and Mulgore."},kw={"albino murloc","barrens","deep fathom ring","devourer","emerald nightmare","murloc","mutanus","naralex","wailing caverns"},rel={"npc:naralex","zone:wailing","topic:emerald-dream","topic:murloc","topic:druid"},src={"Mutanus the Devourer"}}
E["npc:nalpak"] = {t="npc",n="Nalpak",z="wailing",s="Above the Wailing Caverns, Nalpak keeps watch from a cliff-cave. The tauren druid remains faithful to Naralex's vision and guards against the corruption below.",h="Above the Wailing Caverns, Nalpak keeps watch from a cliff-cave.",sec={{t="Watcher Above the Caverns",b="Nalpak watches from a hidden cave above the Wailing Caverns' mouth. He remains loyal to Naralex's vision while his master lies trapped in a corrupted slumber below. To hold back the spreading corruption, Nalpak asks passing adventurers to gather deviate hides for leather.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Nalpak located?",a="Nalpak waits in a cave high on the rock face, directly above the natural formation leading into the Wailing Caverns in the central Barrens.",al={"nalpak location","where is nalpak","find nalpak"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Nalpak?",a="Nalpak is a tauren druid and one of Naralex's Disciples. He watches for twisted creatures emerging from the caverns while Naralex seeks to restore the Barrens through the Emerald Dream.",al={"who is nalpak","nalpak lore"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Nalpak want deviate hides?",a="Nalpak wants to examine the hides of the deviate creatures infesting the Wailing Caverns. Though evil, he believes their unusual hides can serve leatherworkers well.",al={"why deviate hides","deviate hides quest"},it="wants"},{q="What is Nalpak's relationship to Naralex?",a="Nalpak is a faithful student and follower of Naralex. As one of the druid's disciples, he supports Naralex's ambitious attempt to reawaken the springs of the Barrens.",al={"is nalpak naralex disciple","nalpak and naralex"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Nalpak on?",a="Nalpak is a disciple of Naralex and acts in service to the druids seeking to heal the Barrens. While he is a tauren welcoming to those who enter the caverns to aid their cause, his foremost allegiance lies with Naralex's vision and the restoration of the corrupted subterranean springs.",al={"nalpak faction","who does nalpak serve","is nalpak horde"},it="side",add="a6c930b7"},{q="Why is Nalpak at the Wailing Caverns?",a="Nalpak came to the Wailing Caverns alongside Naralex and fellow disciples to channel the Emerald Dream into the arid Barrens. After the ritual went terribly awry, he remained posted near the cavern entrance to enlist adventurers in gathering corrupted materials and dealing with the twisted beasts inside.",al={"why is nalpak here","nalpak wailing caverns reason","what brought nalpak here"},it="why_here",add="ddc6c0b5"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, Nalpak reminds you how perilous the Emerald Dream can be when darkness takes root in a ritual meant to restore the land.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you share Nalpak's devotion to healing Kalimdor's parched lands. He refuses to abandon the mission even after disaster strikes the dreamers."},kw={"barrens druid","deviate hides","disciples of naralex","nalpak","naralex","tauren","wailing caverns"},rel={"npc:naralex","zone:wailing","quest:1486","zone:barrens","topic:tauren"},src={"Nalpak"}}
E["npc:naralex"] = {t="npc",n="Naralex",z="wailing",s="Beneath the Barrens, Naralex sleeps while his dream of green turns to nightmare. The night elf druid sought to restore the parched land through the Emerald Dream, but corruption overtook his slumber and twisted his followers into venomous fiends.",h="Beneath the Barrens, Naralex sleeps while his dream of green turns to nightmare.",sec={{t="A Vision of Green",b="Naralex came to the Barrens with devoted disciples, hoping to restore the forest that covered the plains before the Great Sundering. Beneath the savannah, he found underground springs and rushing geysers. He named the caverns for the howling wind and steam that moaned through the rock. He believed a deep trance could channel the Emerald Dream into those waters, carrying life to the surface and making the wasteland bloom.",sp=0},{t="The Waking Nightmare",b="Deep in the caverns, Naralex entered meditation and reached toward the Emerald Dream. Corruption ensnared his mind instead of the peaceful wild nature he sought. The Emerald Nightmare seized the sleeping druid and made him a conduit for dark energies to enter the living world. Springs turned foul, fungal blooms mutated, and the caverns' beasts became ravenous horrors.",sp=0},{t="Fallen Disciples",b="The Emerald Nightmare's corruption drove Naralex's disciples mad through the psychic backlash of his trance. They abandoned the Cenarion Circle's traditions, took serpent forms, and named themselves the Druids of the Fang. Believing their twisted growth should spread across Kalimdor, they guard Naralex's sleeping body to keep him from waking. A few loyal disciples still seek allies brave enough to break the trance.",sp=1,bt={"q886.5"}}},faq={{q="Who is Naralex?",a="Naralex is a night elf druid of the Cenarion Circle who led an expedition into the Wailing Caverns. He hoped to draw on the Emerald Dream and restore the arid Barrens to the forest that stood there before the Sundering.",al={"naralex lore","who is the sleeping elf","wailing caverns sleeper"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Naralex asleep inside the Wailing Caverns?",a="Naralex entered a meditative trance to channel the Emerald Dream into aquifers beneath the Barrens. A nightmare seized his mind and trapped him in a fevered slumber he cannot escape alone.",al={"why is naralex sleeping","what is naralex doing","naralex trance"},it="why_here"},{q="What created the Druids of the Fang?",a="The Druids of the Fang were once Naralex's faithful disciples. The Emerald Nightmare corrupted his connection to the Dream, and its malice drove them mad. They left the Cenarion Circle, took serpent forms, and guard Naralex's slumber so the corruption can spread.",al={"druids of the fang origin","who are druids of the fang","naralex disciples"},it="threat"},{q="What caused the Wailing Caverns to mutate?",a="Naralex's sleeping body became a conduit for the Emerald Nightmare, whose foul energies seeped into the underground waters. The caverns' plants, crocodiles, raptors, and serpents were warped into aggressive deviate mutants.",al={"why is wailing caverns corrupted","deviate beasts origin","wailing caverns fungus"},it="history"},{q="Can Naralex be awakened?",a="Yes. A loyal Disciple of Naralex works with adventurers willing to enter the depths, defeat the twisted Druids of the Fang, and perform a ritual to break the nightmare's hold on Naralex's mind.",al={"how to save naralex","waking naralex","naralex quest"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why did Naralex want to change the Barrens?",a="Naralex learned that the Barrens had once been a flourishing forest before the Great Sundering shattered Kalimdor. He saw the arid land as a wound and hoped to restore its ancient forest.",al={"why regrow the barrens","naralex barrens goal","why the barrens"},it="wants"},{q="Whose side is Naralex on?",a="Naralex belongs to the Cenarion Circle, making him neutral toward both the Alliance and the Horde. His loyalties lie with the balance of nature rather than the political squabbles of Kalimdor. Unfortunately, his trapped mind has lost control entirely, leaving his slumbering body guarded by twisted former acolytes who attack anyone that enters.",al={"is naralex alliance or horde","naralex faction","who does naralex serve"},it="side",add="ec55d9d1"},{q="Who is Naralex tied to?",a="Naralex is a venerable night elf druid of the Cenarion Circle who brought a retinue of faithful disciples to the Barrens. Most of his followers succumbed to the dark nightmare gripping his mind and transformed into the monstrous Druids of the Fang. A few remain loyal, such as Nalpak and Ebru in the cave above the entrance and a Disciple of Naralex waiting inside the caverns.",al={"naralex allies","naralex disciples","who are naralex's followers"},it="ties",add="4a5a8c9e"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For druids, Naralex's story warns against meddling blindly with primal natural states or reaching too deeply into the Dream without caution. Either can unleash terrible distortions of the wild.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you may see Naralex's effort to heal Kalimdor, yet his ambition in Horde territory disgraced the Cenarion Circle and gave rise to the treacherous Druids of the Fang.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you depend on the oasis pools and wildlife that sustain the tribes of Mulgore and the savannah. The twisted waters beneath the Barrens threaten them.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you face a night elf's failed experiment that has polluted the heart of the Barrens. Horde forces from the Crossroads must contend with rampaging beasts emerging from the caverns."},kw={"cenarion circle","deviate","disciple of naralex","druids of the fang","emerald dream","emerald nightmare","naralex","the barrens","wailing caverns"},rel={"zone:wailing","topic:druids-of-the-fang","topic:emerald-dream","topic:cenarion-circle","topic:druid","zone:barrens","topic:night-elf","quest:1489"},src={"Naralex"}}
E["npc:verdan-the-everliving"] = {t="npc",n="Verdan the Everliving",z="wailing",s="In the Wailing Caverns, Verdan the Everliving lurks in deep tunnels and attacks those who enter. He dwells near the sleeping druid Naralex and the Druids of the Fang.",h="In the Wailing Caverns, Verdan the Everliving lurks in deep tunnels and attacks those who enter.",sec={{t="Beast of the Lush Depths",b="Verdan is the largest bog beast in the overgrown depths of the Wailing Caverns. He is an elemental of foliage, silt, and mire, haunting its flooded hollows. Nothing is known of him from before corruption reached the caverns.",sp=0},{t="Twisted by the Nightmare",b="Verdan roams the depths with the mad Druids of the Fang. Naralex tried to turn the dry Barrens into a lush paradise, but his ritual broke into a vivid nightmare within the Emerald Dream. Corruption seeped through the subterranean waters and tainted every living thing in the cavern.",sp=1,bt={"q886.5"}}},faq={{q="What kind of creature is Verdan?",a="Verdan is a massive bog beast, an elemental animated from plant matter, peat, and subterranean mire.",al={"verdan monster type","what is verdan","verdan race"},it="origin"},{q="Why is Verdan hostile to adventurers?",a="Verdan lurks in the nightmare-tainted depths of the Wailing Caverns, where the sleeping Naralex's dream has turned everything hostile. He treats all who enter as trespassers to crush.",al={"why does verdan attack","verdan hostile","is verdan evil"},it="hostile"},{q="What is Verdan's connection to the Druids of the Fang?",a="Verdan shares the nightmare-tainted caverns with the insane Druids of the Fang. Like them, he is hostile to intruders and guards the deeper reaches.",al={"verdan druids of the fang","verdan fang connection"},it="ties"},{q="Where in the Wailing Caverns is Verdan located?",a="Verdan dwells in a mossy chamber deep along the winding paths of the Wailing Caverns, past several corrupted leaders of the Fang.",al={"where is verdan","verdan location","how to find verdan"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Can Verdan be cured or cleansed?",a="No known way can cleanse Verdan, so adventurers must destroy the hulking beast to pass safely through the cavern.",al={"can verdan be saved","save verdan","purify verdan"}},{q="Why was Verdan called 'the Everliving'?",a="No one knows why Verdan bears the name the Everliving. He is a bog beast of the Wailing Caverns' lush, overgrown depths.",al={"why everliving","everliving meaning","verdan name origin"},it="name"},{q="Who is Verdan the Everliving?",a="Verdan the Everliving is a colossal bog beast, an elemental of plant matter and mire lurking in the overgrown depths of the Wailing Caverns. He dwells amid the nightmare spreading from the sleeping druid Naralex and fiercely attacks any living creature that crosses his path.",al={"who is verdan","verdan the everliving","what is verdan"},it="identity",add="429fb6d1"},{q="Whose side is Verdan the Everliving on?",a="Verdan serves no faction. He lurks in the nightmare-tainted depths alongside the corrupted Druids of the Fang and is just as hostile as they are to any outsiders seeking to disturb the caverns or wake Naralex.",al={"verdan faction","is verdan with the druids","verdan allegiances"},it="side",add="58b439d8"},{q="What does Verdan the Everliving want?",a="Verdan has no grand scheme beyond territorial defense and destruction. He keeps a relentless vigil over the deep caverns, seeking only to crush any trespassers who venture near his lair.",al={"verdan goal","what does verdan want","verdan motive"},it="wants",add="06330139"},{q="Why is Verdan the Everliving here?",a="Verdan dwells in the lush, overgrown depths of the Wailing Caverns, where the nightmare of the sleeping druid Naralex has turned the caverns hostile. Nothing is known of him from before that corruption.",al={"why is verdan in wailing caverns","how did verdan get here","verdan origin here"},it="why_here",add="b1009155"},{q="Why is Verdan the Everliving feared?",a="Verdan is feared as the most physically brutal monster within the Wailing Caverns. His immense size and plant-hewn strength allow him to deliver devastating blows capable of crushing an armored warrior in mere seconds.",al={"why is verdan feared","is verdan dangerous","how strong is verdan"},it="fame",add="357d8159"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Verdan's lair shows what grows in the caverns when the Emerald Dream turns to nightmare.",["class:Shaman"]="Verdan is an elemental spirit of earth and water, warped into violence. Putting him down restores balance to the Barrens' fractured elements.",["faction:Horde"]="The Wailing Caverns lie at the heart of the Barrens. Defeating dangerous beasts like Verdan helps protect nearby crossroads and settlements."},kw={"bog beast","druids of the fang","elemental","everliving","naralex","nightmare","verdan","wailing caverns"},rel={"zone:wailing","npc:naralex","quest:1012","topic:druid"},src={"Verdan the Everliving"}}
E["quest:1486"] = {t="quest",n="Deviate Hides",z="wailing",s="At the Wailing Caverns, Nalpak seeks a use for the strange properties of deviate hides. A disciple of Naralex, he keeps watch above the entrance while his teacher lies trapped in a twisted nightmare. Beneath the Barrens, mutated beasts roam, and Nalpak hopes their skins can serve a practical purpose.",h="At the Wailing Caverns, Nalpak seeks a use for the strange properties of deviate hides.",sec={{t="Corruption Made Manifest",b="Naralex sought to awaken the springs beneath the Barrens and restore life to the dry plains. Instead, the Wailing Caverns became dangerous. The night elf druid's mind slipped into a terrifying nightmare, and that nightmare reached the waking world. Raptors, crocolisks, vipers, and shambling horrors turned vicious and misshapen, warped by emerald corruption leaking from their dreaming master.",sp=0},{t="A Pragmatic Druid",b="From the rock above the cavern mouth, Nalpak watches the disaster with dread and practical curiosity. He knows the deviate beasts are malignant and unnatural, yet their corrupted forms may yield useful materials. Their tough, warped pelts could help skilled leatherworkers. Nalpak hopes to make durable equipment from the fruits of a tragic nightmare.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Nalpak?",a="Nalpak and his fellow disciples camp high on the skull-shaped rock above the Wailing Caverns entrance. Climb the slopes behind the cave mouth, then carefully drop onto the upper ledge in the eye socket overlooking the oasis.",al={"nalpak location","where is nalpak","how to find nalpak","quest giver deviate hides"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What are deviate creatures?",a="Deviate creatures are local beasts transformed by the Emerald Nightmare that escaped from Naralex's slumbering mind. Raptors, snakes, crocolisks, and wind serpents native to the Barrens have become darker and more vicious, with strange magical properties and mottled, unnatural hides.",al={"what are deviates","deviate beasts","why are animals mutated in wailing caverns"},it="target"},{q="Why does Nalpak want these hides?",a="Nalpak believes the corrupted beasts' hides have unusual strength and can be put to practical use. He hopes leatherworkers can study and work the pelts into resilient gear.",al={"why deviate hides","what does nalpak want hides for","purpose of deviate hides"},it="motive"},{q="Can any deviate creature drop the hides?",a="Mutated beasts in the tunnels and interior of the Wailing Caverns carry these skins. Hunters and leatherworkers can find extra pelts by skinning them, beyond those scavenged from their remains.",al={"which mobs drop deviate hides","who drops deviate hide","deviate hide farm"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Is Nalpak aligned with the Horde or the Alliance?",a="Nalpak is a tauren druid and one of the Disciples of Naralex. He remains neutral and accepts aid from any capable adventurer, Alliance or Horde, brave enough to enter the corrupted caves.",al={"is nalpak horde","is deviate hides alliance","can alliance do deviate hides"},it="side"},{q="What happened to Naralex?",a="Naralex sought to awaken the Barrens' underground springs by joining his consciousness to the Emerald Dream. The Nightmare seized his slumber instead, turning the caverns into a breeding ground for horrors and leaving him comatose deep within them.",al={"who is naralex","naralex nightmare","what happened to the druid in wailing caverns"},it="history"},{q="What is the Deviate Hide for?",a="Deviate hides possess strange, otherworldly properties born from the nightmare corrupting the caverns. While the creatures they come from are twisted and hostile, Nalpak believes their unusual pelts can be repurposed through leatherworking to craft sturdy armor and packs, bringing something useful out of the corruption.",al={"deviate hide use","why gather deviate hides","deviate hide purpose"},it="item",add="58e10be2"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you can see Nalpak's camp as the surviving disciples' grim vigil over an effort gone terribly wrong. For fellow druids, containing the cavern's mutations is personal.",["profession:Herbalism"]="As an herbalist, you know the abnormal growth feeding the deviate beasts is tied to corrupted flora and underground springs winding through the cavern network."},kw={"barrens","deviate","deviate hides","emerald nightmare","leatherworking","nalpak","naralex","wailing caverns"},rel={"npc:nalpak","zone:wailing","npc:naralex","zone:barrens"},m={start="Nalpak",level="17",faction="Neutral",id=1486,ri={"Deviate Hide"}},src={"Deviate Hides (Classic)"}}
E["quest:1487"] = {t="quest",n="Deviate Eradication",z="wailing",s="In the Wailing Caverns, Ebru sends you to thin the deviate beasts. The night elf druid watches over the caverns while other disciples try to wake Naralex. His twisted vision has spawned mutated creatures whose numbers threaten to carry corruption beyond the underground springs and into the Barrens.",h="In the Wailing Caverns, Ebru sends you to thin the deviate beasts.",sec={{t="A Dream Gone Terribly Wrong",b="Naralex brought his followers to the Barrens' underground springs, hoping to draw on the Emerald Dream and restore the dry plains as woodland. Instead, the Dream ensnared him, and his sleep turned to nightmare. Power coursing through the caverns warped native plants and animals into aggressive mutants called deviate beasts.",sp=0},{t="Ebru's Stand",b="Ebru watches from a cliffside cave above the entrance with the few Disciples of Naralex who remain. Their numbers dwindle. Some work to wake their fallen leader, but Ebru sees danger in the deviate vipers, shamblers, ravagers, and dreadfangs. They multiply quickly and may spread into the Barrens. So Ebru asks you to enter the deep tunnels and cull the monsters at their source.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do I find Ebru to start this quest?",a="Ebru waits with a few other Disciples of Naralex in a secluded cave high above the Wailing Caverns' main entrance. The cave lies in what looks like the right eye socket of the skull-shaped rock. Climb around the mountain ridge, then carefully descend to the upper ledge.",al={"ebru location","where is ebru","how to get to ebru","wailing caverns eye cave"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What caused the beasts to become deviate?",a="The beasts changed when Naralex's effort to renew the Barrens went wrong. He linked his mind to the underground springs and the Emerald Dream, but a nightmare seized his thoughts and twisted the restorative power into a force that mutates local wildlife.",al={"why are they deviate","deviate beasts origin","what corrupted the animals in wc"},it="origin"},{q="Who are the Disciples of Naralex?",a="The Disciples of Naralex are druids who followed him to the Wailing Caverns to help restore the Barrens. After the Nightmare trapped Naralex, many disciples became feral or lost their minds. Only a small remnant remains sane and tries to undo the disaster.",al={"disciples of naralex","naralex followers","who are the druids in wailing caverns"},it="people"},{q="Can Alliance and Horde both take this quest?",a="Yes. Ebru and the druids with her seek to preserve nature and contain the Nightmare. They accept help from capable champions of either the Horde or the Alliance.",al={"deviate eradication alliance or horde","is deviate eradication neutral"},it="side",gp=true},{q="What creatures do you have to slay for Ebru?",a="Ebru asks you to hunt four kinds of corrupted creatures deep in the caverns: Deviate Ravagers, Deviate Vipers, Deviate Shamblers, and Deviate Dreadfangs. You must slay seven of each.",al={"deviate eradication mobs","deviate eradication targets","which deviate to kill"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Does completing this quest wake Naralex?",a="No. Ebru asks you to thin the dangerous beasts and limit the damage they cause. Waking Naralex takes a separate ritual deep in his sanctum at the heart of the cavern.",al={"does this wake naralex","how to wake naralex"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does Ebru want the deviate beasts destroyed?",a="While other Disciples of Naralex focus their efforts on awakening their trapped master, Ebru sees an immediate threat festering within the Wailing Caverns. Naralex's vision of restoring the Barrens back into a lush forest has devolved into a nightmare, spewing corrupt, unnatural creatures throughout the tunnels. Ebru believes there is no hope of healing these lands or saving their leader until these twisted beasts are purged from the caverns.",al={"ebru motive","why kill deviate beasts","why does ebru want deviate beasts dead"},it="motive",add="62e049f1"},{q="What are the deviate creatures in the Wailing Caverns?",a="They are the local fauna—vipers, raptors, and shambling plant horrors—warped into monstrous forms by the dark energies leaking from Naralex's nightmare. Naralex sought to channel the Emerald Dream to revitalize the arid Barrens, but when his dream turned foul, the ambient magical spillway mutated the wildlife into aggressive, unnatural predators that now infest the cavern depths.",al={"what are deviate ravagers","deviate beasts wailing caverns","corrupt creatures wailing caverns"},it="target",add="b4bfe70b"},{q="Why can't the Disciples of Naralex clear the caverns themselves?",a="The disciples are stretched far too thin to mount an assault on their own. Their order has dwindled significantly since Naralex became ensnared in his nightmare, and those few who remain are divided between preparing a ritual to awaken him and defending what little foothold they still maintain. They lack the numbers and martial strength to push into the caves and exterminate the beasts without outside assistance.",al={"why does ebru need my help","why cant disciples clear caves","disciples of naralex why need help"},it="why_me",add="ab17f40e"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, the twisted life in the caverns warns what can happen when communion with the Emerald Dream goes wrong.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can help protect nearby settlements such as the Crossroads by culling the predators in the Wailing Caverns, at the heart of Kalimdor's central plains.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you may feel bound to aid your stranded kin as Naralex's noble hope becomes a nightmare-born horror."},kw={"barrens","deviate dreadfang","deviate eradication","deviate ravager","deviate shambler","deviate viper","ebru","naralex","wailing caverns"},rel={"npc:ebru","npc:naralex","zone:wailing","zone:barrens","topic:emerald-dream"},m={start="Ebru",level="21",faction="Neutral",id=1487},src={"Deviate Eradication"}}
E["quest:1489"] = {t="quest",n="Hamuul Runetotem",z="wailing",s="Tonga Runetotem sends you to Thunder Bluff as a strange taint spreads through the Barrens. He suspects the Wailing Caverns lie at its heart and seeks Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem’s counsel.",h="Tonga Runetotem sends you to Thunder Bluff as a strange taint spreads through the Barrens.",sec={{t="A Disturbing Dream",b="Near the Barrens’ oases, Tonga Runetotem found creatures marked by a strange affliction. An unnatural taint covered their shells, and Tonga came to believe the land itself was caught in a troubled dream. He suspects the waters flowing from the Wailing Caverns are to blame. Entering those caverns calls for more wisdom than one naturalist can offer.",sp=0},{t="Counsel on Elder Rise",b="Tonga sends you to Thunder Bluff for counsel from his kin, Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem. Hamuul is the highest-ranking tauren druid and a revered spiritual leader of the Cenarion Circle in Mulgore. From Elder Rise, he watches for disturbances across Kalimdor. He confirms the nightmare spreading through the Barrens is a dire threat, calling for the full might of Horde champions.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Tonga send me to Hamuul?",a="Tonga found a strange affliction among creatures near the Barrens’ oases and suspects the Wailing Caverns’ waters are its source. He sends you to Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff for Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem’s counsel before anyone enters the caverns.",al={"why hamuul","why talk to hamuul","hamuul quest purpose"},it="motive"},{q="Where is Hamuul Runetotem located?",a="Hamuul Runetotem is atop Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff, the tauren capital in Mulgore. Other druids and shamans dwell there with him, overlooking the surrounding plains.",al={"hamuul location","where is hamuul","find hamuul runetotem"},gp=true},{q="What is the source of the taint Tonga noticed?",a="Tonga suspects underground springs in the Wailing Caverns are the source of the taint. Their strange waters corrupt local wildlife and flora, leaving the land seeming trapped in an inescapable nightmare.",al={"what is the taint","oasis corruption","wailing caverns taint"},it="threat"},{q="What happens after speaking with Hamuul?",a="Hamuul welcomes you to Thunder Bluff and prepares you for what lies ahead. He warns that facing the nightmare beneath the Barrens is a dire undertaking, then directs you to Nara Wildmane to prepare for the descent into the Wailing Caverns.",al={"next quest after hamuul","what next","hamuul follow up"},it="next_step"},{q="Who is Hamuul Runetotem?",a="Hamuul Runetotem leads the tauren druids and is a close childhood friend and advisor to High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof. Since the Third War, he has learned the ways of the wild and guides tauren druids in communion with nature and the Cenarion Circle.",al={"who is hamuul","hamuul lore","archdruid hamuul"},it="identity"},{q="Is this quest required to enter the Wailing Caverns?",a="No. You can enter the Wailing Caverns without attunement, but this Horde story ties the mystery of the Barrens’ lush oases to the expedition inside the caverns.",al={"wailing caverns attunement","is this quest mandatory"},gp=true},{q="Why does Tonga Runetotem ask an adventurer to go to Hamuul?",a="Tonga Runetotem is stationed in the Crossroads to actively monitor the strange, disturbing changes spreading through the Barrens and its oases. Because he must remain in the field studying the corrupted wildlife firsthand, he relies on capable travelers to carry his reports and seek guidance directly from Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem on the Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff.",al={"why send me to hamuul","why cant tonga go to hamuul","why me tonga"},it="why_me",add="a40fa735"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a tauren druid, you come to Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem as a student of the mentor who established modern tauren druidism under Malfurion Stormrage’s teachings.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you see the concerns of your ancestral hunting grounds in the Barrens brought before the tribal elders atop Mulgore’s sacred bluffs.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know the Barrens is a crossroads for the young Horde. Investigating the spreading taint protects supply lines between Durotar, Mulgore, and the northern outposts."},kw={"elder rise","hamuul runetotem","oases","taint","the barrens","thunder bluff","tonga runetotem","wailing caverns"},rel={"npc:tonga-runetotem","subzone:elder-rise","zone:thunderbluff","zone:wailing","zone:barrens","topic:druid"},m={start="Tonga Runetotem",["end"]="Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem",level="16",faction="Horde",id=1489},src={"Hamuul Runetotem (quest)"}}
E["quest:1490"] = {t="quest",n="Nara Wildmane",z="wailing",s="In Thunder Bluff, Nara Wildmane helps the Horde grasp the danger in the Wailing Caverns. Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem saw corruption in the Emerald Dream but could not endure it, so he sent travelers to his young disciple. Nara saw the nightmare taking hold of their kin.",h="In Thunder Bluff, Nara Wildmane helps the Horde grasp the danger in the Wailing Caverns.",sec={{t="A Vision of Corruption",b="Unnatural signs spread across the Barrens, and Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem entered the Emerald Dream to find their cause. There he found a druidic cult that had once hoped to restore life to the dry savannah. A vile taint had driven its members mad.\n\nAge kept Hamuul from enduring the nightmare’s assault, so he fled to the waking world. His younger disciple, Nara Wildmane, refused to leave so soon. Her fierce resolve kept her in the dreamscape, where she saw the transformed cult for herself.",sp=0},{t="Confronting the Nightmare",b="Nara Wildmane knows what the fallen druids have done and what they mean to unleash upon Kalimdor. When she saw them in the Emerald Dream, their faces were twisted and scaled like serpents. Hamuul guides the Cenarion Circle from Thunder Bluff, while Nara brings the knowledge needed to fight the corruption. Now the Horde strikes into the Wailing Caverns to destroy the leaders who forsook their sacred oaths.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Nara Wildmane?",a="Nara Wildmane is a young tauren druid who lives on the Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff. She studies under Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem and faces the nightmares corrupting nature.",al={"who is nara","nara wildmane lore","nara wildmane thunder bluff"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Hamuul Runetotem send travelers to speak with her?",a="Hamuul Runetotem sends travelers to Nara because age and failing strength kept him from remaining in the corrupted dream. Young and fiercely determined, Nara stayed longer and learned of the Druids of the Fang and their plans.",al={"why speak with nara","hamuul to nara","why hamuul send me here"},it="motive"},{q="What did Nara see in the Emerald Dream?",a="Nara saw the fallen druids dwelling in the Wailing Caverns. Their faces had become scaled and serpentine, and she learned of their crimes and dark plots against the Barrens.",al={"what did nara see","nara dream vision","scaled druids dream"}},{q="Where can Nara Wildmane be found?",a="Nara Wildmane can be found in a druidic tent atop the Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff, across from Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem.",al={"where is nara","nara wildmane location","find nara wildmane"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after reporting to Nara Wildmane?",a="After you speak with Nara, she directs you into the Wailing Caverns to slay the rogue Druids of the Fang. This leads to the larger undertaking called Leaders of the Fang.",al={"next quest after nara","what does nara want me to do","leaders of the fang follow up"},it="next_step"},{q="Why are the druids in the Wailing Caverns corrupted?",a="Led by Naralex, the druids entered the caverns hoping to draw on the Emerald Dream and bring lush life to the Barrens. Naralex’s slumber became a horrific nightmare that ensnared his followers and twisted them into the serpentine Druids of the Fang.",al={"wailing caverns cult","druids of the fang why evil","why barrens druids evil"},it="threat"},{q="Why does Hamuul Runetotem ask you to speak with Nara instead of going himself?",a="Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem is burdened by old age and the toll of reaching into the spirit realm. When he entered the Emerald Dream to investigate the troubles in the Wailing Caverns, his strength failed, forcing him to pull back. Nara Wildmane is young and fierce, remaining in the dreaming long after he fled. Because Hamuul is in Thunder Bluff coordinating the tauren druids and cannot afford to spend what little vitality he has running errant messages or facing the threat alone, he entrusts capable travelers to learn what Nara discovered.",al={"why hamuul send me to nara","why can't hamuul speak to nara","why send an adventurer to nara"},it="why_me",add="2cdff5a8"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren who has recently taken up druidism under Hamuul, you are part of a young generation willing to face unnatural blight, as Nara is.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you can admire Nara’s courage in the corrupted reaches of the Emerald Dream, where even the veteran Hamuul could not linger.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can see how Nara’s watchfulness guards its heartland against the dark energies twisting the Barrens and threatening to spread into Mulgore."},kw={"barrens","druids of the fang","elder rise","emerald dream","hamuul runetotem","nara wildmane","thunder bluff","wailing caverns"},rel={"zone:wailing","quest:914","topic:druid","zone:barrens"},m={start="Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem",["end"]="Nara Wildmane",level="16",faction="Horde",id=1490},src={"Nara Wildmane (quest)"}}
E["quest:1491"] = {t="quest",n="Smart Drinks",z="wailing",s="In Ratchet, Mebok Mizzyrix seeks a new formula for his drink. His brew of powdered Sunscale raptor horns disappointed him, so he now wants ectoplasmic residue from the Wailing Caverns.",h="In Ratchet, Mebok Mizzyrix seeks a new formula for his drink.",sec={{t="A Recipe for Disaster",b="Mebok Mizzyrix sells goods in Ratchet and hopes to make a fortune with a drink that sharpens the mind. His first formula used powdered Sunscale raptor horns, but the brew disappointed him. Now he has turned to the strange essence seeping from the Wailing Caverns, hoping it will make his drink succeed.",sp=0},{t="The Wailing Essence",b="Strange changes have come to the Barrens. New oases have appeared, and local wildlife has grown aggressive and warped. Mebok suspects a substance he calls Wailing Essence is behind them. He sends you into the cavern labyrinth to destroy its oozing ectoplasms and gather their glowing fluid in bottles for his formula.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Mebok Mizzyrix?",a="Mebok Mizzyrix is a goblin merchant in Ratchet. He hopes to sell an intellect-boosting drink across Kalimdor and make a fortune.",al={"mebok mizzyrix","who gives smart drinks","smart drinks quest giver"},it="identity"},{q="Why didn't the raptor horns work?",a="Mebok thought powdered horns from Sunscale raptors would make an intellect-boosting brew, but the drink disappointed him. Now he has turned to a more dangerous ingredient.",al={"why raptor horns failed","raptor horn drink"},it="history"},{q="What is Wailing Essence?",a="Wailing Essence is ectoplasmic fluid from strange slimes deep inside the Wailing Caverns. Mebok believes it causes the unusual changes to plants and animals spreading through the Barrens.",al={"what is wailing essence","essence from wailing caverns"},it="item"},{q="Where do you find the ectoplasms carrying the essence?",a="You can gather the essence from evolving, devouring, and nightmare ectoplasms in the underground tunnels of the Wailing Caverns, west of Ratchet.",al={"where are ectoplasms","smart drinks mobs","who drops wailing essence"},gp=true},{q="Is the smart drink safe to consume?",a="The essence comes from nightmarish slimes linked to corrupting mutations across the Barrens, so bottling it as a tonic is reckless. Mebok cares more about selling the drink than keeping customers safe.",al={"is smart drink poisonous","does the drink work"},it="power"},{q="What comes after completing Smart Drinks?",a="After you deliver Wailing Essence, Mebok considers his immediate beverage venture complete. He rewards you and promises a share of future profits if his tonic makes him a fortune.",al={"smart drinks follow up","what next after smart drinks"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Mebok Mizzyrix want the Wailing Essence?",a="Mebok Mizzyrix is an ambitious goblin entrepreneur in Ratchet determined to strike it rich. After his initial attempt using raptor horns failed to produce an intellect-enhancing beverage, he pivoted to a far more volatile ingredient. Believing that the strange mutations warping the Barrens' flora and fauna stem from the potent energies within Wailing Essence, he intends to brew it directly into his concoctions and sell them as miraculous smart drinks for immense personal profit.",al={"mebok motive","why does mebok want smart drinks","why make smart drinks"},it="motive",add="b3462a0e"},{q="What are the ectoplasms carrying the essence?",a="The ectoplasms are strange, ooze-like manifestations dwelling deep within the Wailing Caverns. As volatile, corrupted energies pool beneath the oasis fissures, the local subterranean essence congeals into evolving, devouring, and nightmarish spectral slimes. These mindless entities absorb the primal, mutagenic hum of the caverns, concentrating the strange Wailing Essence inside their shifting forms until harvested.",al={"what ectoplasms","wailing caverns ectoplasm","who holds the essence"},it="target",add="6730f7d3"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="If you cook, raw ectoplasm tainted by nightmare is a poor choice for a drink. Mebok wants to steep it into a tonic despite the danger to food safety.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you enter the Wailing Caverns to cleanse the nightmare twisting the emerald dreamscape. Mebok sees that ecological taint as cheap syrup for his business.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can find quick coin among the Barrens' crossroads merchants in Ratchet. Mebok's business asks you to deliver monster parts without many questions."},kw={"barrens","ectoplasm","mebok mizzyrix","raptor horns","ratchet","smart drinks","wailing caverns","wailing essence"},rel={"npc:mebok-mizzyrix","quest:865","zone:wailing","subzone:ratchet","zone:barrens"},m={start="Mebok Mizzyrix",level="18",id=1491,ri={"Wailing Essence"}},src={"Smart Drinks"}}
E["quest:6981"] = {t="quest",n="The Glowing Shard",z="wailing",s="Deep in the Wailing Caverns, you find a green shard whose smoky depths stir unease. Its mystery draws you to Ratchet and onward.",h="Deep in the Wailing Caverns, you find a green shard whose smoky depths stir unease.",sec={{t="A Disturbing Discovery",b="You carry a green crystal from deep within the Wailing Caverns. Beneath its bright, solid face, shadowy wisps seem to churn. Those who touch it feel uneasy, and its strange presence hints at the corruption around the sleeping druids and their nightmare-haunted sanctuary.",sp=0},{t="Seeking Answers in Ratchet",b="In Ratchet, the shard's origin remains unclear. Engineer Sputtervalve examines it, but goblin machinery and ordinary geology cannot explain its nature. He points you toward the rocky ridges above the caverns, where Falla Sagewind, a tauren mystic, watches over the troubled spirits of the Barrens.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Glowing Shard?",a="You found the Glowing Shard deep within the Wailing Caverns. Faint smoky shapes swirl beneath its glassy surface and unsettle those who study it.",al={"glowing shard item","what is this green gem","shard from wailing caverns"},it="item"},{q="Who can examine the shard in Ratchet?",a="Engineer Sputtervalve near Ratchet's flight master can examine the shard. Its strange energy leads him to point you toward someone with spiritual knowledge.",al={"who in ratchet looks at shard","ratchet npc for shard","sputtervalve shard"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Where is Falla Sagewind located?",a="Falla Sagewind keeps her camp on the mountain peaks directly above the Wailing Caverns entrance in the central Barrens.",al={"falla sagewind location","where is falla","mountain above wailing caverns"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Does Sputtervalve have a quest marker over his head?",a="No. Sputtervalve has no active icon above his head. Speak with him and choose the dialogue about the strange glowing shard to continue.",al={"sputtervalve no question mark","cant turn in to sputtervalve","sputtervalve bugged"},gp=true},{q="Why does the shard look like it contains smoke?",a="The smoke-like swirl reflects corruption spreading through the Wailing Caverns. It is bound to the Emerald Nightmare invading the thoughts of the sleeping Druids of the Fang.",al={"why does shard smoke","green smoke in gem","corruption in shard"},it="power"},{q="Who can complete the quest chain after Falla Sagewind?",a="Horde and Alliance adventurers can both follow the story. Falla Sagewind's findings lead to In Nightmares, where heroes seek guidance from their own leaders and elders.",al={"is this quest horde only","alliance glowing shard","who gets in nightmares"},sp=1,it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why do you need to investigate the Glowing Shard?",a="The glowing shard is deeply unsettling. Solid yet filled with swirling, smoky green depths, it exudes an unnatural presence that demands explanation. Having recovered it from the heart of the troubled Wailing Caverns, you need to understand what corruption it carries and what threat it might pose to the Barrens.",al={"why investigate the glowing shard","glowing shard motive","why take the shard to ratchet"},it="motive",add="8f9c92be"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you may see the shard's emerald sheen and smoky heart as grim signs of the Emerald Nightmare reaching the waking world through your fallen brethren in the Wailing Caverns.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you know the Barrens' balance matters to the Shu'halo. Bringing this unnatural relic to Falla Sagewind can help reveal the corruption poisoning your ancestral lands.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can help uncover the shard's mystery and guard the Barrens' crossroads and trade routes from threats festering in the underground springs.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance explorer far from home in Kalimdor, you can see the danger in a dark power corrupting nature beneath the Barrens."},kw={"barrens","druids of the fang","emerald nightmare","falla sagewind","glowing shard","ratchet","sputtervalve","wailing caverns"},rel={"zone:wailing","npc:sputtervalve","npc:falla-sagewind","quest:3369","subzone:ratchet","topic:goblin","topic:horde","topic:alliance"},m={start="Glowing Shard",["end"]="Falla Sagewind",level="26",id=6981},src={"The Glowing Shard"}}
E["quest:914"] = {t="quest",n="Leaders of the Fang",z="wailing",s="In the Wailing Caverns, four leaders of the Druids of the Fang threaten the Barrens. Nara Wildmane sends Horde champions from Thunder Bluff to slay them and take their twisted dream gems. If the druids are not stopped, their serpentine nightmare may claim the land.",h="In the Wailing Caverns, four leaders of the Druids of the Fang threaten the Barrens.",sec={{t="A Vision Corrupted",b="Naralex, a night elf druid, entered the Wailing Caverns' underground springs. He hoped the Emerald Dream would bring life back to the dry Barrens. But when he fell asleep, his dream became a nightmare. The acolytes who came with him abandoned nature's harmony and fell under its corruption. They became the Druids of the Fang.",sp=0},{t="The Four Dream Gems",b="Four leaders of the Druids of the Fang carry dream gems that channel warped dream energy. They hope to reshape the Barrens into their own viperous Eden. Lord Cobrahn, Lady Anacondra, Lord Pythas, and Lord Serpentis each carry one gem. While the gems remain with them, corruption spreads through Kalimdor's soil and waters.",sp=0},{t="A Burden Lifted in Thunder Bluff",b="From Thunder Bluff, Nara Wildmane watches over nature's balance, yet the caverns' torment reaches her mind. The four serpent lords and their gems hold the sect together. Taking the gems breaks their command and frees Nara from lingering nightmares. It also protects the surrounding plains from unnatural blight.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who are the leaders of the Druids of the Fang?",a="The Druids of the Fang are led by four fallen druids: Lady Anacondra, Lord Cobrahn, Lord Pythas, and Lord Serpentis. They abandoned their original nature teachings, took serpent forms, and wield nightmare magic in the Wailing Caverns.",al={"leaders of the fang names","wailing caverns bosses","who leads druids of the fang"},it="target"},{q="What are the dream gems?",a="Each of the four leaders in the Wailing Caverns carries a dream gem. The gems focus the nightmare-tainted energy from Naralex's slumber and fuel the sect's efforts to change the Barrens.",al={"what are the gems","gem of cobrahn","dream gems lore"},it="item"},{q="Why does Nara Wildmane want the gems?",a="Nara Wildmane is a tauren druid in Thunder Bluff who feels the nightmare's spiritual ripples. The corrupted leaders haunt her dreams, and she wants their power broken to protect her mind and the Barrens.",al={"who is nara wildmane","why kill the leaders","nara wildmane motive"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Were the Druids of the Fang always evil?",a="No. The Druids of the Fang were once noble night elf druids who followed Naralex into the caverns to heal the dry savanna. When Naralex fell into a nightmare, its energies warped their minds and made them a fanatical snake cult.",al={"druids of the fang origin","why did the druids turn bad","naralex disciples"},it="history"},{q="Where is this quest turned in?",a="You bring all four gems to Nara Wildmane on the Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff. After gathering them in the Wailing Caverns, you travel back to Mulgore to deliver them.",al={"leaders of the fang turn in","where is nara wildmane","hand in leaders of the fang"},gp=true},{q="Does killing the leaders cure Naralex?",a="Slaying the four leaders breaks the sect's upper ranks and halts the spread of their ritual, but Naralex does not wake from this alone. Other druidic rites deeper in the caverns are needed to awaken him.",al={"does this save naralex","killing leaders effect"}},{q="Why does Nara Wildmane want the Druids of the Fang killed?",a="The Druids of the Fang are former Cenarion Circle druids who set out to restore the lushness of the Barrens, but their minds became warped by the Emerald Nightmare. Now they seek to remake the land into their own twisted dreamscape. Their corruption plagues Nara's own thoughts and dreams, and she fears that unless their four leaders are slain and their influence broken, the entire Barrens will fall to a dark and cursed future.",al={"nara wildmane motive","why kill druids of the fang","why does nara want them dead"},it="motive",add="5ca16cf2"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a tauren druid, you may feel the Druids of the Fang's corruption deeply. They twist the Emerald Dream into poisonous blight, an affront to Cenarion principles.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know the Barrens connects Orgrimmar, Thunder Bluff, and the Darkspear isles. Serpent worshipers changing the land threaten the stability of the whole Horde.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you hold the Earth Mother's health at the heart of your faith. Corruption spreading from the Barrens' springs profanes the land you roam."},kw={"anacondra","barrens","cobrahn","dream gems","leaders of the fang","nara wildmane","pythas","serpentis","wailing caverns"},rel={"zone:wailing","topic:druids-of-the-fang","quest:1490","zone:barrens","zone:thunderbluff","topic:druid"},m={start="Nara Wildmane",level="22",faction="Horde",id=914,ri={"Gem of Anacondra","Gem of Cobrahn","Gem of Pythas","Gem of Serpentis"}},src={"Leaders of the Fang"}}
E["quest:959"] = {t="quest",n="Trouble at the Docks",z="wailing",s="In Ratchet, a stolen bottle puts Bigglefuzz's job at risk. Mad Magglish fled inland with a 99-Year-Old Port, a gift from Baron Revilgaz to Gazlowe, and now hides in the Wailing Caverns.",h="In Ratchet, a stolen bottle puts Bigglefuzz's job at risk.",sec={{t="A Clumsy Mishap",b="Ratchet's docks carry sea trade with Booty Bay across the Great Sea. One morning, a huge shipment arrived, and Crane Operator Bigglefuzz overloaded his crane to unload it faster. The crane dropped the whole load across the docks. In the confusion, Mad Magglish, a local nuisance, snatched a valuable bottle of liquor and fled inland.",sp=0},{t="Diplomatic Vintage",b="The bottle is a 99-Year-Old Port, a personal diplomatic gift from Baron Revilgaz, Booty Bay's ruler, to Gazlowe, Ratchet's chief engineer and overseer. Its loss could humiliate Bigglefuzz and anger both trade leaders. Fearing for his job or worse, Bigglefuzz followed the thief to the mouth of the Wailing Caverns. But fear stopped him from going inside.",sp=0},{t="The Cavern Hideout",b="Mad Magglish hides in damp natural tunnels outside the Wailing Caverns' inner gateway, not deep in the corrupted dreamscape. The thief relies on clumsy stealth and dark alcoves, hoping pursuers will give up. Find Magglish in the outer caverns before the port is uncorked or destroyed.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is this bottle of port so important?",a="The 99-Year-Old Port is a lavish personal gift from Baron Revilgaz of Booty Bay to Gazlowe, Ratchet's boss. Losing it could anger Ratchet's leadership and cost Crane Operator Bigglefuzz his livelihood.",al={"why does bigglefuzz care","what is the 99-year-old port","why is the wine important"},it="item"},{q="Who is Mad Magglish?",a="Mad Magglish is a thief and troublemaker who hangs around Ratchet. When Bigglefuzz dropped a huge cargo load on the docks, Magglish grabbed the rare port and fled to hide in the nearby Wailing Caverns.",al={"who is magglish","who stole the port","mad magglish lore"},it="target"},{q="Do I have to enter the Wailing Caverns dungeon to find the thief?",a="No. Mad Magglish hides in the winding cave passages outside the instance portal, using poor stealth in the upper side tunnels or near the flooded chambers by the main entrance.",al={"is magglish inside the instance","where is mad magglish","find magglish"},gp=true},{q="How did the cargo spill happen?",a="A huge cargo shipment arrived from Booty Bay, and Crane Operator Bigglefuzz tried to unload more crates at once than his equipment could handle. The overloaded crane dropped the load across Ratchet's docks.",al={"why did the crates drop","what did bigglefuzz do","crane mishap ratchet"},it="origin"},{q="What is the relationship between Ratchet and Booty Bay?",a="Ratchet and Booty Bay are Steamwheedle Cartel port towns, joined by commerce and privateer fleets. Regular shipments and formal courtesies pass between Baron Revilgaz in the south and Gazlowe in the Barrens, sustaining their shared trade empire.",al={"ratchet and booty bay connection","steamwheedle ports","revilgaz and gazlowe"},it="ties"},{q="Why didn't Bigglefuzz retrieve the bottle himself?",a="Bigglefuzz followed the thief to the Wailing Caverns' entrance, but the underground labyrinth's eerie reputation and monstrous inhabitants frightened him into stopping at the threshold.",al={"why didn't the goblin get it","why did bigglefuzz stop chasing"},it="why_me"},{q="Why does Crane Operator Bigglefuzz need this port back?",a="Bigglefuzz's job is on the line. When he tried to unload more crates than his crane could handle, the entire morning shipment from Booty Bay collapsed. In the chaos, the prized bottle of ninety-nine-year-old port went missing, and the dockmaster has been breathing down his neck ever since. Because the vintage was a personal gift meant for Ratchet's chief engineer, Gazlowe, failing to recover it means Bigglefuzz is facing immediate dismissal.",al={"why does bigglefuzz want the port","bigglefuzz motive","why help bigglefuzz"},it="motive",add="b908c2b9"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you can spot Mad Magglish's careless concealment in the cavern crannies, where the thief uses rudimentary stealth to escape notice.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help Ratchet's dockhands keep the primary neutral port between Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms running smoothly.",["faction:Alliance"]="As a member of the Alliance, you travel deep in the Horde-dominated Barrens, where good relations with Steamwheedle port operators help ensure safe passage through neutral waters."},kw={"bigglefuzz","booty bay","gazlowe","magglish","port","ratchet","revilgaz","wailing caverns"},rel={"npc:crane-operator-bigglefuzz","subzone:ratchet","zone:wailing","npc:baron-revilgaz","subzone:booty-bay","zone:barrens"},m={start="Crane Operator Bigglefuzz",level="18",id=959,ri={"99-Year-Old Port"}},src={"Trouble at the Docks"}}
E["quest:962"] = {t="quest",n="Serpentbloom",z="wailing",s="Deep in the Wailing Caverns, Serpentbloom draws Apothecary Zamah’s attention. She seeks more specimens for the Royal Apothecary Society’s research and the Forsaken.",h="Deep in the Wailing Caverns, Serpentbloom draws Apothecary Zamah’s attention.",sec={{t="Eyes of the Apothecary",b="Apothecary Zamah watches the Pools of Vision beneath Thunder Bluff’s Spirit Rise. She came from the Undercity as an envoy of the Royal Apothecary Society. Her tauren hosts tend to spiritual balance and the wounded land, while Zamah studies rare and virulent materials. She has isolated a sample of Serpentbloom and seeks more for Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and the Forsaken’s research.",sp=0},{t="The Depths of the Caverns",b="Serpentbloom grows in the damp, twisting grottos of the Wailing Caverns, far from the Barrens’ open sun. The corrupted druids of the Fang have twisted these humid depths, where serpentine denizens guard the plant. Many scouts sent by Zamah failed to return. Now she seeks hardy adventurers to gather more.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Apothecary Zamah?",a="Apothecary Zamah is a researcher and envoy of the Royal Apothecary Society from the Undercity. She watches the Pools of Vision beneath Thunder Bluff’s Spirit Rise and links Forsaken alchemists with the wider continent of Kalimdor.",al={"zamah","apothecary zamah lore","who gives serpentbloom"},it="identity"},{q="Why does the Royal Apothecary Society want Serpentbloom?",a="Zamah believes Serpentbloom holds chemical potential when refined in large quantities. The Society seeks rare, potent plants across Kalimdor to aid the Forsaken’s alchemical experiments.",al={"why serpentbloom","forsaken herb research","purpose of serpentbloom"},it="item"},{q="Where does Serpentbloom grow?",a="Serpentbloom grows in damp caverns beneath the northern Barrens, within the Wailing Caverns’ rock corridors and passages.",al={"where is serpentbloom","serpentbloom location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why haven't previous scouts returned?",a="The Wailing Caverns are overrun by devolved beasts, raptors, and the corrupted Druids of the Fang. Inexperienced foragers were quickly overwhelmed by predators and venomous defenders in the winding tunnels.",al={"missing scouts","zamah's scouts","is wailing caverns dangerous"},it="threat"},{q="Do the Tauren approve of Zamah's research?",a="The tauren of Thunder Bluff gave the Forsaken sanctuary out of sympathy and a desire to heal them. The Royal Apothecary Society’s alchemy can approach unnatural experimentation, troubling traditional shamans and druids.",al={"tauren reaction","spirit rise apothecaries"},it="conflict"},{q="Does harvesting Serpentbloom require herbalism skills?",a="No. Any adventurer willing to brave the Wailing Caverns can pluck Serpentbloom from the cave floor without herbalism training.",al={"do i need herbalism","gather serpentbloom profession"},gp=true},{q="Why does Apothecary Zamah want Serpentbloom gathered?",a="Apothecary Zamah was dispatched to Thunder Bluff by the Royal Apothecary Society on a specific assignment to further the interests of the Forsaken and the Dark Lady, Lady Sylvanas Windrunner. Having analyzed a rare sample of Serpentbloom, Zamah sees immense potential in its properties if obtained in substantial quantities. Securing enough specimens allows her research to advance the scientific and alchemical ambitions of the Undercity.",al={"apothecary zamah motive","why does zamah need serpentbloom","why gather serpentbloom"},it="motive",add="962715c8"},{q="Why does Apothecary Zamah send an adventurer instead of gathering Serpentbloom herself?",a="Zamah cannot easily abandon her station in Thunder Bluff, and harvesting the herb requires venturing into the treacherous, corrupted depths of the Wailing Caverns. She has already dispatched several scouts and agents into the cave system on her behalf, but none of them returned alive. She needs seasoned, capable adventurers willing to brave those dark recesses where ordinary scouts failed.",al={"why send me serpentbloom","why doesn't zamah get serpentbloom","why adventurers for serpentbloom"},it="why_me",add="92b49307"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Gathering Serpentbloom supports the Royal Apothecary Society’s alchemical work in Lordaeron, under the Dark Lady’s mandate.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you see Horde hospitality in the welcome given Forsaken apothecaries beneath the Spirit Rise. Their lethal concoctions contrast with traditional earth healing.",["profession:Herbalism"]="The twisted Wailing Caverns nurture flora found nowhere else on the Barrens’ sunbaked surface.",["faction:Horde"]="This work strengthens the early alliance between the Undercity and the Kalimdor tribes. They share resources and rare reagents across the ocean."},kw={"apothecary","barrens","royal apothecary society","serpentbloom","spirit rise","thunder bluff","undercity","wailing caverns","zamah"},rel={"quest:853","topic:royal-apothecary-society","zone:wailing","zone:thunderbluff","topic:forsaken","zone:undercity","zone:barrens"},m={start="Apothecary Zamah",level="18",faction="Horde",id=962,ri={"Serpentbloom"}},src={"Serpentbloom (quest)"}}
E["subzone:cavern-of-mists"] = {t="subzone",n="Cavern of Mists",z="wailing",s="Geysers veil the way into the Wailing Caverns from the Cavern of Mists.",h="Geysers veil the way into the Wailing Caverns from the Cavern of Mists.",sec={{t="The Threshold of the Nightmare",b="You cross the Cavern of Mists on the way to the Wailing Caverns' deeper heart. Geysers burst through the floor and feed a deep pool at the center. Warm vapor cloaks the ledges and water, where raptors, serpents, oozes, and threshadons roam. Trigore the Lasher, a rare hydra, prowls here too. Such creatures mark the unnatural growth deeper below.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Cavern of Mists?",a="Cavern of Mists forms the outer caves of the Wailing Caverns, southwest of the Crossroads in the Barrens. You cross this chamber to reach the portal into the deeper caves.",al={"cavern of mists location","where is cavern of mists","wailing caverns entrance cave"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is it called the Cavern of Mists?",a="Geysers burst through the stone floor, feeding the central pool and filling the cavern with humid fog.",al={"why misty","cavern of mists name origin"},it="name"},{q="What creatures live here?",a="Raptors, oozes, wind serpents, snakes, toads, and threshadons live around the pool. The rare hydra Trigore the Lasher is sometimes seen there too.",al={"mobs in cavern of mists","cavern of mists monsters"},it="residents"},{q="Who is Trigore the Lasher?",a="Trigore the Lasher is a dangerous rare hydra, sometimes found swimming with the threshadons in the central pool.",al={"trigore","hydra rare wailing caverns"}},{q="What is the Cavern of Mists?",a="The Cavern of Mists, also referred to as the Wailing Cavern, is the outer subterranean chamber preceding the deeper reaches of the Wailing Caverns. Fed by active geysers that erupt from the stone floor, the cavern features a verdant central pool where warm water and vapor mingle, filling the enclosed subterranean air with a perpetual, heavy fog.",al={"what is cavern of mists","cavern of mists lore","about cavern of mists"},it="place",add="923aae57"},{q="Is the Cavern of Mists dangerous?",a="Yes, the chamber is perilous for unwary travelers. Wild predators prowl the misty banks and murky waters, including aggressive raptors, creeping oozes, venomous snakes, and snapping wind serpents. The deep central pool is home to predatory threshadons, alongside monstrous threats such as the elusive hydra known as Trigore the Lasher.",al={"is cavern of mists dangerous","cavern of mists danger","threats in cavern of mists"},it="danger",add="8ec0c6f8"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a Cenarion druid, you see the twisted wildlife in these heavy vapors as a warning: Naralex's communion with the Emerald Dream has gone badly astray.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know that clearing predatory beasts from these mists helps secure the trade routes and outposts around the Crossroads."},kw={"barrens","cavern of mists","geysers","threshadons","trigore the lasher","wailing caverns"},rel={"zone:wailing"},src={"Cavern of Mists"}}
E["subzone:crag-of-the-everliving"] = {t="subzone",n="Crag of the Everliving",z="wailing",s="The Crag of the Everliving lies beneath a canopy of corrupted growth in the Wailing Caverns. Lord Pythas holds its central reaches, and an ancient being dwells in the heights above.",h="The Crag of the Everliving lies beneath a canopy of corrupted growth in the Wailing Caverns.",sec={{t="A Corrupted Canopy",b="Twisted growth fills the Crag of the Everliving, fed by the Nightmare corrupting Naralex's sleep. Mossy platforms rise over winding paths where Deviate Shamblers prowl. These living plant hulks crowd the undergrowth.\n\nLord Pythas watches the crag's central reaches. Once a disciple of Naralex, he abandoned his druidic vows for the venomous rites of the Druids of the Fang.",sp=0},{t="The Ancient Guardian",b="Verdan the Everliving gives the chamber its name. This colossal, primordial plant elemental dwells in the crag's upper heights, corrupted by the Emerald Nightmare gripping the cavern. No longer a peaceful guardian of nature, Verdan now forms a fearsome line of defense.\n\nBeyond Verdan's towering form waits Lord Serpentis. He calls himself chief of the Fanglords and oversees the sect's descent into serpentine madness.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does this area get its name?",a="The chamber takes its name from Verdan the Everliving, an ancient, colossal plant beast in the crag's highest terraces. Once nature's timeless vitality made manifest, he has fallen under the Nightmare's sway.",al={"why crag of the everliving","everliving name origin","crag name"},it="name"},{q="Who controls this part of the caverns?",a="Lord Pythas presides over the crag. On higher ledges above him lurk Verdan the Everliving and Lord Serpentis, leader of the Druids of the Fang.",al={"who is in charge here","crag boss","fanglord here"},it="in_charge"},{q="What creatures are commonly found in the Crag of the Everliving?",a="Deviate Shamblers overrun the crag, alongside twisted serpents and fanatical Druids of the Fang. The Shamblers are plant horrors born from the corrupted springs.",al={"monsters in crag","crag enemies","what lives here"},it="residents"},{q="Why is plant life thriving so deep underground?",a="Naralex, a night elf druid, harnessed the underground springs to rejuvenate the Barrens. The Emerald Nightmare ensnared his ritual, driving wild growth rampant and twisting it into hostile, aberrant flora.",al={"why are there plants underground","why so green","corrupted greenery"},it="origin"},{q="What is the Crag of the Everliving?",a="The Crag of the Everliving is a lush, verdant subterranean cavern deep within the Wailing Caverns. Fed by corrupted natural energies, it is characterized by flourishing plant life, rampant growth, and towering rock shelves.",al={"what is crag of the everliving","crag of the everliving info","about crag of the everliving"},it="place",add="6a6b08ee"},{q="Is the Crag of the Everliving dangerous?",a="Yes, it is among the deadliest portions of the caverns. Deviate Shamblers stalk the overgrown terraces, and the crag is defended by corrupted druids of the Fang, presided over by Lord Pythas and near the lair of Lord Serpentis.",al={"how dangerous is crag of the everliving","is crag of the everliving dangerous","threats in crag of the everliving"},it="danger",add="cca8a755"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For Cenarion druids, the Crag of the Everliving is a tragic lesson: the Nightmare has turned nature's vitality and elemental guardianship into lethal tools.",["profession:Herbalism"]="The crag's humid, dream-soaked soil and unnaturally lush underground air nourish rare roots and mushrooms."},kw={"barrens","crag of the everliving","deviate shamblers","druids of the fang","lord pythas","lord serpentis","verdan","wailing caverns"},rel={"zone:wailing","npc:lord-pythas","npc:verdan-the-everliving","npc:lord-serpentis"},src={"Crag of the Everliving"}}
E["subzone:dreamer-s-rock"] = {t="subzone",n="Dreamer's Rock",z="wailing",s="At Dreamer's Rock, Naralex sleeps while the Barrens still wait for renewal. He came to restore the land through the Emerald Dream, but his communion now feeds a nightmare.",h="At Dreamer's Rock, Naralex sleeps while the Barrens still wait for renewal.",sec={{t="The Slumber of Naralex",b="At the heart of the Wailing Caverns, Naralex lies in a chamber like a night elf barrow den. He entered a deep trance to reach the underground springs and channel the Emerald Dream into the Barrens' dry soil. Dark forces seized that connection, and his nightmare now twists the chamber's wildlife. His followers became the venomous Druids of the Fang, and terrible aberrations spill into the waking world.",sp=0},{t="The Awakening Ritual",b="A surviving Disciple of Naralex can reach Dreamer's Rock and perform the waking ritual once the corruption of the Fanglords ends. As the chant begins, Naralex's lingering nightmare sends monstrosities to guard its hold on his sleeping mind. Mutanus the Devourer is the final horror of this psychic torment. The aberration rises from the depths of the dreamer's subconscious to consume those who seek to free him.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is sleeping at Dreamer's Rock?",a="Naralex, a night elf druid, sleeps at Dreamer's Rock. He came to the Wailing Caverns to use its underground water channels to restore life to the Barrens, but nightmares seized his communion with the Emerald Dream.",al={"sleeping elf","who is asleep here","who is naralex","dreamer identity"},it="residents"},{q="Why is this chamber called Dreamer's Rock?",a="The chamber takes its name from Naralex, known as 'the Dreamer.' Like a night elf barrow den, it holds his resting body while his spirit travels through the Dream.",al={"why dreamers rock","dreamers rock name meaning","name origin"},it="name"},{q="What happens when you try to wake Naralex?",a="After the Fanglords are defeated, a surviving Disciple of Naralex attempts the waking ritual. The ritual brings horrors from Naralex's nightmare to guard his sleeping mind.",al={"waking naralex","disciple ritual","naralex event"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why did Naralex's followers turn hostile?",a="Naralex's nightmare warped his followers' minds. They abandoned their Cenarion vows, embraced serpent aspects, and became the Druids of the Fang, guarding their master's tormented, unending sleep.",al={"druids of the fang origin","why are the druids evil","corrupted druids"},it="conflict"},{q="What is Dreamer's Rock?",a="Dreamer's Rock is a secluded natural chamber deep within the Wailing Caverns, lying beyond the Screaming Gully. Functioning much like a traditional druidic barrow den, it serves as the resting site where the night elf druid Naralex entered his deep slumber to channel the Emerald Dream into the Barrens.",al={"what is dreamers rock","dreamers rock chamber","where is dreamers rock"},it="place",add="8278540a"},{q="What happened at Dreamer's Rock?",a="Naralex came to this chamber to tap into the Emerald Dream and restore verdant life to the arid Barrens. Instead, a dark corruption seeped into his vision, twisting his noble slumber into a waking nightmare. The horrors from his disturbed mind manifested into flesh and broke free into the cavern, corrupting his followers and the surrounding springs.",al={"dreamers rock history","what happened to naralex here","how did dreamers rock fall"},it="history",add="29a7d0a7"},{q="Is Dreamer's Rock dangerous?",a="It is exceptionally dangerous. The chamber sits at the heart of the cavern's corruption, directly exposed to Naralex's twisted subconscious. Any attempt to disturb or awaken the sleeping druid draws forth malevolent nightmare aberrations eager to keep him ensnared, including the monstrous horror known as Mutanus the Devourer.",al={"how dangerous is dreamers rock","dreamers rock threats","is it safe at dreamers rock"},sp=1,it="danger",add="70f268b5"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you can see the danger in Naralex's attempt to reach the Emerald Dream. Noble intent can meet horrors that slumber within.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you find a sacred barrow-style chamber corrupted beneath the arid Barrens. Naralex and his followers took tragic risks far from Kalimdor's northern forests."},kw={"barrow den","dreamer's rock","dreamers rock","druids of the fang","emerald dream","mutanus","naralex","wailing caverns"},rel={"npc:naralex","zone:wailing","npc:mutanus-the-devourer","subzone:screaming-gully","topic:druid","topic:night-elf"},src={"Dreamer's Rock"}}
E["subzone:screaming-gully"] = {t="subzone",n="Screaming Gully",z="wailing",s="Steam and wind make Screaming Gully howl beneath the northern Barrens, at the Wailing Caverns’ entrance.",h="Steam and wind make Screaming Gully howl beneath the northern Barrens, at the Wailing Caverns’ entrance.",sec={{t="Threshold of the Nightmare",b="Past the entrance, wind groans through the deep fissures of Screaming Gully. Damp growth and humid mist fill the cavern, far from the dry Barrens above. Lady Anacondra, a Fanglord, watches over the acolytes of the Druids of the Fang and fierce deviate raptors. Ancient snapping turtles patrol the shallow waters below, including Kresh.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Screaming Gully located?",a="Screaming Gully lies just beyond the portal inside the Wailing Caverns, beneath the northern Barrens.",al={"screaming gully location","where is screaming gully","how to find screaming gully"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is it called the Screaming Gully?",a="Steam and wind vent through fissures in the rock, making the Wailing Caverns howl and moan. The wide entrance chasm catches the sound and carries its cries.",al={"why screaming gully","screaming gully name origin"},it="name"},{q="Who rules over the Screaming Gully?",a="Lady Anacondra, a Fanglord corrupted by the Emerald Nightmare alongside Naralex, oversees the chamber.",al={"screaming gully boss","who is in screaming gully","screaming gully leader"},it="residents"},{q="What creatures roam this chamber?",a="Deviate raptors, corrupted Druids of the Fang and aquatic creatures roam the gully. The ancient turtle Kresh wanders its flooded floor.",al={"screaming gully mobs","enemies in screaming gully"},it="danger"},{q="What is the Screaming Gully?",a="The Screaming Gully is the first sprawling subterranean chamber encountered just beyond the threshold of the Wailing Caverns. Fed by underground streams that pool into shallow waters along its floor, this cavernous rift echoes with eerie natural sounds and the hiss of corrupted wildlife, serving as the front line of the nightmare taking root within the depths.",al={"what is screaming gully","screaming gully overview","screaming gully lore"},it="place",add="edd75ba3"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a Cenarion druid, you find fallen brethren here. They left the path of claw and sky for serpentine corruption."},kw={"barrens","deviate raptor","fanglords","kresh","lady anacondra","screaming gully","wailing caverns"},rel={"zone:wailing","npc:lady-anacondra","topic:druids-of-the-fang","topic:druid"},src={"Screaming Gully"}}
E["zone:wailing"] = {t="dungeon",n="Wailing Caverns",z="wailing",s="Beneath the Barrens' Lushwater Oasis, trapped steam whistles through the Wailing Caverns. Springs and fissures once promised to revive Kalimdor's sun-bleached savanna. Now the caverns hold poisoned waters, twisted wildlife, and fallen disciples caught in an unnatural nightmare.",h="Beneath the Barrens' Lushwater Oasis, trapped steam whistles through the Wailing Caverns.",sec={{t="A Noble Vision Turned Poisonous",b="The night elf druid Naralex found a vast system of underground waters and sought to restore the Barrens. Through a conduit into the Emerald Dream, he meant to draw pure primal life through the springs and turn the parched savanna into a thriving paradise.\n\nDeep in the caverns, Naralex entered communion with the Dream, anchored by his loyal acolytes. But his sleeping mind touched the Emerald Nightmare. Corruption seized him, and his conduit became a valve pouring venom and madness into the waters.",sp=0},{t="The Druids of the Fang",b="As the Nightmare's dark energy spread from Naralex's helpless form, his students' minds fell to madness. They forsook the tranquil wisdom of the Cenarion Circle and became the fanatical Druids of the Fang.\n\nTheir leaders, Lady Anacondra, Lord Cobrahn, Lord Pythas, and Lord Serpentis, take reptilian forms. They embrace the caverns' venomous mutation instead of fighting it, and shield their sleeping master from outside interference. They believe this twisted growth is nature's true evolution.",sp=0},{t="The Nightmare Made Flesh",b="Breaking the Druids of the Fang's hold does not save Naralex. At Dreamer's Rock, his remaining uncorrupted disciples begin a ritual to gently rouse him from his trance. His sleeping mind thrashes, and its deepest terror erupts as Mutanus the Devourer, a monstrous, distorted murloc. Mutanus is the flesh of Naralex's worst nightmares.\n\nOnly by slaying Mutanus can the channel to the Nightmare be snapped. Naralex is freed to wake, assume avian form, and fly from the tainted caves.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is it called the Wailing Caverns?",a="The Wailing Caverns take their name from the mournful cries heard in their tunnels. Trapped subterranean steam and high-pressure gusts of wind force their way through tight limestone fissures, making the eerie whistle.",al={"why wailing caverns","name origin","why do they wail"},it="name"},{q="What caused the beasts inside to become 'deviate'?",a="When Naralex fell under the Emerald Nightmare's sway, tainted dream energies flowed into the underground springs. The contaminated waters mutated the raptors, crocolisks, and serpents living there into unnatural deviate forms.",al={"deviate corruption","why are raptors mutate","deviate beasts origin"},it="threat",nx={11}},{q="Who are the Druids of the Fang?",a="The Druids of the Fang were once Naralex's devoted night elf and tauren acolytes. Corrupted alongside him by the Nightmare, their minds shattered, and their druidic arts turned to worship of serpents and venom. They took titles such as Cobrahn, Pythas, and Anacondra.",al={"fang druids","druids of the fang lore","who is serpentis"},it="people"},{q="Why is the final boss a giant murloc named Mutanus?",a="Mutanus appears during the attempt to awaken Naralex. The ritual reveals Mutanus's nature and connection to the sleeping druid.",al={"why mutanus murloc","what is mutanus","final boss lore"},sp=1,it="target"},{q="What happens after Mutanus is defeated?",a="The disciples' attempt to awaken Naralex continues after the confrontation. The ritual reveals the druid's fate at its end.",al={"waking naralex","naralex ending","what happens to naralex"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Who is living in the cave above the cavern entrance?",a="Cenarion Circle loyalists, including Nalpak and Ebru, live in the cavern's skull-like rock eye socket above the entrance. They seek brave travelers to gather deviate hides and cleanse the corruption before it engulfs the Barrens.",al={"cave above entrance","snake skull eye npcs","who is nalpak and ebru"},it="residents"},{q="What is the Wailing Caverns?",a="The Wailing Caverns are an expansive underground cave network running beneath the arid Barrens, near the Lushwater Oasis. Its natural subterranean springs channel water for miles under the earth, feeding the rare surface oases scattered across the region. Discovered by the night elf druid Naralex, it was meant to be the heart of a grand project of natural regrowth. Instead, it became an epicenter of dangerous corruption after a tragic catastrophe took hold of the druids within.",al={"what is wailing caverns","wailing caverns overview","about wailing caverns"},it="place",add="3386ab3f"},{q="Who lives down there?",a="The caverns teem with unnatural wildlife and rogue druids. Naralex's corrupted followers, the Druids of the Fang, have claimed the tunnels as their domain alongside mutated serpents, oozes, raptors, and crocolisks. Outside the instance gate, wild beasts, oozes, and even outcasts lurk in the damp passages, while the corrupted druids guard the inner chambers and protect their sleeping master.",al={"who is in wailing caverns","wailing caverns creatures","inhabitants of wailing caverns"},it="residents",add="e070a543"},{q="Why did the Horde send me here?",a="The strange mutation of local beasts and the foul energies bubbling out of the Lushwater Oasis threaten the entire Barrens. The Horde and the Cenarion druids of Thunder Bluff cannot tolerate an uncontrolled dark power poisoning the land and waterways right on the doorstep of the Crossroads. You were sent to investigate, put an end to the rogue leaders of the Fang, and help quell the growing danger.",al={"why am i in wailing caverns","horde wailing caverns mission","why send me to wailing caverns"},it="arrival",add="49d47201"},{q="Is this part of a bigger problem in the Barrens?",a="Yes. The subterranean channels beneath these caves feed the surface oases across the Barrens. The Nightmare's taint corrupting the waters within the caverns has begun spilling out into the surrounding landscape, causing wild creatures like raptors and crocolisks to mutate and turning the Lushwater Oasis into a breeding ground for strange deviate life.",al={"barrens oasis problem","deviate corruption barrens","is wailing caverns affecting the barrens"},it="conflict",add="d445bb78"},{q="Are the deviates spreading outside the caverns?",a="They already are. The underground springs flow directly into surface oases like Lushwater, bringing unnatural growth and mutated creatures out into the open savannah. Strange creatures like Deviate Fish can be pulled from the waters outside, and aggressive mutated predators increasingly harass travelers between the oases and the Crossroads.",al={"are deviates spreading","deviate beasts barrens","deviate fish outside"},it="threat",add="038fd1cf"},{q="Who is in charge down here?",a="While Naralex lies trapped in his corrupted slumber deep within the caves, the daily rule of the caverns belongs to the Druids of the Fang. They are led by Lord Serpentis, once Naralex's finest student, who rallied his twisted brethren to remake the land into their own warped paradise alongside other fang lords like Cobrahn, Pythas, and Lady Anacondra.",al={"who leads wailing caverns","wailing caverns leader","boss of wailing caverns"},it="in_charge",add="8502642f"},{q="What is the Emerald Dream and how does it connect to this cave?",a="The Emerald Dream is a vast spirit realm representing Azeroth untouched and wild, stewarded by the green dragonflight and accessible to druids. Naralex believed he could channel the pure, restorative energies of the Dream into the underground aquifers of the Wailing Caverns to restore lush plant life to the Barrens. However, when he tapped into it, he was ensnared by the Emerald Nightmare, projecting a twisted version of nature into the physical caves.",al={"emerald dream connection","wailing caverns emerald dream","naralex emerald dream"},it="history",add="32be29c8"},{q="Why is everyone so worried about this place?",a="The subterranean springs in the caverns feed the primary oases that sustain life across the arid Barrens. If the Emerald Nightmare's taint continues to seep into those waterways unchecked, the twisted mutations and madness corrupting the cave's flora and fauna could spread across the entire region, turning the land into a waking horror.",al={"why worry about wailing caverns","wailing caverns threat to barrens","how bad is wailing caverns"},it="threat",add="38e519c2"},{q="How did I end up in Wailing Caverns?",a="You traveled south from the Crossroads into the Lushwater Oasis, following reports of bizarre beasts and corrupted waters bleeding through the Barrens. Tucked behind the lush foliage and Kolkar centaur camps sits a massive, skull-shaped cavern carved into the rock. Drawn by calls for aid from Thunder Bluff, Ratchet goblins seeking odd essences, or disciples camped in the skull's eye above, you descended past the winding fissures and hiss of underground geysers into the groaning depths below.",al={"how did i get here","how do i reach wailing caverns","where did i come from to get here"},it="arrival",add="81917ac6"},{q="What am I supposed to be doing in Wailing Caverns?",a="You are here to purge the corruption that has gripped this underground spring. The night elf druid Naralex fell into a nightmarish slumber trying to revitalize the Barrens, twisting the creatures within and driving his disciples into the venomous Druids of the Fang. You must hunt down the four Fanglords—Lady Anacondra, Lord Cobrahn, Lord Pythas, and Lord Serpentis—to break their grip, and then help the remaining disciple awaken Naralex before his fevered nightmare consumes the oasis completely.",al={"what is my goal here","why am i in wailing caverns","what am i doing down here"},it="purpose",add="28a012f3"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For druids of both Cenarion tradition and the tauren walk, the caverns are a tragic warning of the perils within the Emerald Dream. Purging their fallen brethren, the Druids of the Fang, is a solemn duty.",["race:Tauren"]="The twisted waters threaten the fragile oases that sustain life across the Barrens. Cleansing the springs is vital to the tribes of Mulgore and the Crossroads.",["race:NightElf"]="Naralex was revered among night elf druids. His corruption by the Emerald Nightmare is a painful catastrophe for his kin across the sea."},kw={"deviate","druids of the fang","emerald nightmare","lady anacondra","lord cobrahn","lord pythas","lord serpentis","lushwater oasis","mutanus","naralex","verdan"},rel={"npc:naralex","topic:druids-of-the-fang","npc:mutanus-the-devourer","quest:914","subzone:lushwater-oasis","topic:emerald-dream","npc:lord-serpentis","zone:barrens"},m={levels="17-24"},src={"Wailing Caverns"}}
